1
00:00:02,230 --> 00:00:07,425
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 2

2
00:00:07,791 --> 00:00:09,783
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki;

3
00:00:10,745 --> 00:00:13,089
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:13,128 --> 00:00:19,339
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:29,643
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) sent Sohail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) to negotiate with Rasool Allah ﷺ a truce.

6
00:00:30,007 --> 00:00:32,100
When Rasool Allah ﷺ saw Sohail(سُهيل), he said;

7
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:33,990
 سَهُلَ عَلَيْكُمْ اَمْرُكُمْ

8
00:00:34,522 --> 00:00:36,186
Your matter has become easy.

9
00:00:36,226 --> 00:00:40,579
Because the name Sohail(سُهيل) is derived from Sahula(سَهُلَا), which means easy.

10
00:00:40,779 --> 00:00:46,228
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ took it, as a good omen from the name that Tafa'ul(تفاعل) which is called the Tafa'ul(تفاعل)

11
00:00:46,519 --> 00:00:53,809
that peace is on its way, and that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are intending on reaching an agreement.

12
00:00:54,245 --> 00:00:59,270
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Sohail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو) they deliberated for a while, on the terms of the agreement

13
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:06,564
 and they were very insistent, on not allowing Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه) to enter Makkah that year.

14
00:01:06,603 --> 00:01:08,956
They were very persistent on this particular point

15
00:01:09,003 --> 00:01:13,802
and this is the zeal of Jahilliyah(جاهلية), and the pride of Jahilliyah(جاهلية), the arrogance of Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

16
00:01:13,842 --> 00:01:18,230
They didn't want people to say that he entered it upon us forcefully,

17
00:01:18,785 --> 00:01:22,368
and Rasool Allah ﷺ tried to argue with them, this point to, no avail.

18
00:01:22,415 --> 00:01:23,560
They completely refused.

19
00:01:23,681 --> 00:01:28,258
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted a settlement, Rasool Allah ﷺ he mentioned before

20
00:01:28,951 --> 00:01:31,694
لَا يَدْعُوْنِيْ اِلاَ خُطَّهْ يَعْظُّمُوْنَ بِهَا

21
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:39,513
They would not call me, to any plan in which the sanctities are glorified, but I would accept it.

22
00:01:40,494 --> 00:01:43,950
Now, the terms of the agreement were spoken verbally.

23
00:01:44,415 --> 00:01:46,979
So, the only thing left was to write them down.

24
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:51,971
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was very upset with what he heard.

25
00:01:52,308 --> 00:01:54,293
So, he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

26
00:01:54,824 --> 00:01:57,509
Aren't you the Messenger of Allah? Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes.

27
00:01:57,777 --> 00:01:59,828
Aren't we, the Muslims? He said, Yes.

28
00:02:00,191 --> 00:02:02,732
Aren't they, the disbelievers.? He said: Yes.

29
00:02:02,981 --> 00:02:04,050
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

30
00:02:04,090 --> 00:02:06,697
فَعَلَامَ نُعْطِي الدَّنِيَّةَ فِيْ دِيْنِنَا اِذَّنْ

31
00:02:06,739 --> 00:02:09,826
Then why should we demean our religion then?

32
00:02:09,953 --> 00:02:15,191
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw this as lowering our status and lowering our position.

33
00:02:15,467 --> 00:02:18,809
You are the Messenger of Allah, so you represent Al-Haqq(ألحق).

34
00:02:19,081 --> 00:02:21,086
 They are the Mushrikeen(مشركين), they represent evil.

35
00:02:21,317 --> 00:02:23,510
We are the Muslims, who are followers of Haqq(ألحق).

36
00:02:23,823 --> 00:02:28,130
Why should we bargain with them, and why should we reach an agreement with them, to start with?

37
00:02:28,292 --> 00:02:31,148
This was the understanding, the perception of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

38
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:33,093
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Umar(عُمَر);

39
00:02:33,308 --> 00:02:38,119
اَنَا عَبْدُاللهِ وَرَسُولُهْ، لَن أخَالِفَ اَمْرَه’ وَلَنْ يُّضَيِّعَنِيْ

40
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:41,121
I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger,

41
00:02:41,342 --> 00:02:45,398
I will not disobey Him and He will not abandon me.

42
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:49,416
Umar(عُمَر) then went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and said: Isn't he Rasool Ullah? He said: Yes.

43
00:02:49,647 --> 00:02:51,168
Aren't we the Muslims? He said: Yes.

44
00:02:51,399 --> 00:02:53,431
Aren't they, the disbelievers? He said: Yes.

45
00:02:53,662 --> 00:02:55,650
فَعَلَامَ نُعْطِي الدَّنِيَّةَ فِيْ دِيْنِنَا اِذَّنْ

46
00:02:55,675 --> 00:02:58,196
Then why should we demean our religion.

47
00:02:58,472 --> 00:02:59,099
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said;

48
00:02:59,131 --> 00:03:00,423
 اِلْزَمْ غَرْزَةْ

49
00:03:00,463 --> 00:03:01,539
Follow him,

50
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,221
أَنَه، رَسُوْلُ الله

51
00:03:03,261 --> 00:03:07,142
He is the messenger of Allah and Allahعَزّوجَلّ will not forsake him.

52
00:03:07,795 --> 00:03:12,068
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) later on, would regret, these arguments of his.

53
00:03:12,148 --> 00:03:14,412
 Even though, they were, they were made with good intention.

54
00:03:14,452 --> 00:03:19,988
 But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was very sensitive, when it comes to Haqq(ألحق),

55
00:03:20,218 --> 00:03:21,543
 that's why, he is  called Al-Farooq(ألفاروق).

56
00:03:21,903 --> 00:03:23,940
He distinguishes between right and evil.

57
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:30,249
And he always submits his desires and his intention is to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

58
00:03:30,567 --> 00:03:34,314
He does not allow himself to follow, the whims of the Nafs(نفس).

59
00:03:35,009 --> 00:03:39,588
He was a very strong believer, Mo'min Al-Qawwi(مؤمن القوي).

60
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:44,495
So, he would control himself and he only argued here

61
00:03:44,744 --> 00:03:49,902
because of his intentions to give Nusra(نصرة), victory to the religion of Allah.

62
00:03:50,306 --> 00:03:54,273
However, when he saw that the matter, is a matter of revelation

63
00:03:54,582 --> 00:03:57,537
that Rasool Allah ﷺ has instructions from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

64
00:03:58,142 --> 00:04:03,282
He realized his mistake and he said, he would later on, remember this and say;

65
00:04:03,892 --> 00:04:10,382
So I have gone on fasting, giving alms, praying and freeing slaves,

66
00:04:10,628 --> 00:04:16,037
 because of what I did that day, and out of fear for what I said, that day.

67
00:04:16,259 --> 00:04:17,087
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says:

68
00:04:17,111 --> 00:04:19,054
إِنَّ الْحَسَنَاتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ

69
00:04:19,226 --> 00:04:21,270
The Good deeds erases bad deeds.

70
00:04:21,369 --> 00:04:23,556
So, if you commit a mistake, if you make a sin.

71
00:04:23,751 --> 00:04:26,710
Do a lot of good deeds, after it, in order to erase that sin.

72
00:04:26,750 --> 00:04:28,027
See Umar(عُمَر) here is saying;

73
00:04:28,181 --> 00:04:32,424
I was doing fasting, giving Sadaqah(صدقه), praying voluntary prayer,

74
00:04:32,464 --> 00:04:36,023
 and freeing slaves and this is one of the greatest deeds to free slaves.

75
00:04:36,238 --> 00:04:37,895
He was doing it to erase that sin.

76
00:04:38,156 --> 00:04:41,749
So, this is what, we should do, because all of us are going to commit sins.

77
00:04:42,550 --> 00:04:43,592
This is our nature.

78
00:04:44,152 --> 00:04:47,490
Therefore, we need to erase those sins with good deeds.

79
00:04:48,229 --> 00:04:52,605
They started writing the terms of the agreement and these terms were;

80
00:04:52,967 --> 00:04:57,388
Both have agreed to complete truce for a period of 10 years,

81
00:04:57,673 --> 00:05:02,962
during which all the people will enjoy peace and security and will not attack one another.

82
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:09,613
Next, if anyone from the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) joins Muhammad(محمد) without permission from his guardian or chief,

83
00:05:09,688 --> 00:05:12,164
he shall be returned to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

84
00:05:12,586 --> 00:05:19,510
Next, if anyone from the camp of Muhammad(محمد) joins Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they are not required to return him.

85
00:05:19,698 --> 00:05:22,152
 See here, if somebody comes from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), he is returned

86
00:05:22,207 --> 00:05:24,510
 but if somebody comes from Muhammad(محمد) he is not returned.

87
00:05:25,088 --> 00:05:28,283
This was one of the conditions that were displeasing to the Muslims.

88
00:05:28,935 --> 00:05:33,204
Both sides agree that they harbor good intentions towards each other.

89
00:05:33,229 --> 00:05:35,904
Next, no theft or treachery shall be condoned.

90
00:05:36,027 --> 00:05:42,174
Next, whoever wishes to enter into an alliance with Muhammadﷺ may do so.

91
00:05:42,325 --> 00:05:46,510
And whoever, wants to enter into an alliance with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) may do so.

92
00:05:46,819 --> 00:05:53,676
And finally, it is further agreed that you Muhammad(محمد) shall return home this year, without entering Makkah.

93
00:05:53,763 --> 00:05:58,297
 At the end of one year, we shall evacuated Makkah for you,

94
00:05:58,502 --> 00:06:03,402
so that you may enter it with your followers to stay for three days only.

95
00:06:03,757 --> 00:06:08,476
You shall carry only the armament necessary for a traveler,

96
00:06:08,715 --> 00:06:13,805
namely your swords in their sheaths, you should not carry any other arms.

97
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:21,336
They wrote that down and it's time to sign the agreement and have witnesses

98
00:06:21,958 --> 00:06:25,014
and suddenly Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) appears.

99
00:06:25,054 --> 00:06:26,324
Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) who is he?

100
00:06:26,379 --> 00:06:30,793
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) he's the son of Sohail(سهيل), who is writing the agreement with Muhammadﷺ.

101
00:06:31,368 --> 00:06:35,944
He fled from Makkah, he was in chains,

102
00:06:36,431 --> 00:06:40,145
he was imprisoned in Makkah because of being a Muslim,

103
00:06:40,414 --> 00:06:42,451
he heard the news that the Muslims are near,

104
00:06:42,854 --> 00:06:49,640
so he made it, walking through the valleys or mountain passes until, he reaches to Al-Hudaybiyya(اَلحُدَيبية).

105
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:53,944
And finally, he's happy that he's with the Muslim camp.

106
00:06:54,178 --> 00:06:59,818
Sohail Ibn Amr(سُهَيل بن عمرو) see's him and said: This is the first person, who's case I pick up,

107
00:07:00,194 --> 00:07:01,757
you must return him to me.

108
00:07:02,606 --> 00:07:03,484
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

109
00:07:03,524 --> 00:07:04,286
 اَجِزْهُوْلِيْ

110
00:07:04,326 --> 00:07:05,556
Allow me to have him?

111
00:07:05,757 --> 00:07:07,940
He said: Either this or nothing,

112
00:07:08,551 --> 00:07:10,600
if you refuse to give Abu Jandal(أبوجندل),

113
00:07:11,205 --> 00:07:13,158
I refuse the agreement.

114
00:07:13,219 --> 00:07:14,409
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

115
00:07:14,589 --> 00:07:16,256
We still didn't sign it yet.

116
00:07:16,314 --> 00:07:21,591
Sohail(سُهَيل) was persistent and he refused to back down.

117
00:07:22,049 --> 00:07:24,574
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, to Abu Jandal(أبوجندل);

118
00:07:24,906 --> 00:07:26,218
You must be returned.

119
00:07:26,449 --> 00:07:27,753
Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) said;

120
00:07:27,961 --> 00:07:32,032
O Rasool Ullah you send me back to the disbelievers to test me in my religion.

121
00:07:32,591 --> 00:07:34,586
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

122
00:07:34,984 --> 00:07:39,619
Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) be patient and endure your situation for Allah's sake.

123
00:07:40,051 --> 00:07:42,826
He will certainly provide for you,

124
00:07:43,051 --> 00:07:47,391
and those who are suffering with you, a way out of your hardship.

125
00:07:48,046 --> 00:07:52,540
We have made a peace agreement with these people, giving them a pledge by Allah

126
00:07:52,736 --> 00:07:55,838
that we will be faithful to the terms of our agreement,

127
00:07:56,151 --> 00:07:58,593
we should not violate our pledges.

128
00:07:58,851 --> 00:08:04,601
Umar رضي الله عنه was walking next to Abu Jandal(أبوجندل), when he was being dragged away

129
00:08:05,504 --> 00:08:09,143
and he was pointing the handle of his sword,

130
00:08:09,768 --> 00:08:13,576
placing it, pushing it, next to Abu Jandal(أبوجندل)

131
00:08:13,981 --> 00:08:20,195
with the intention of allowing Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) to pick up the sword and strike his father.

132
00:08:20,519 --> 00:08:21,557
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) says;

133
00:08:21,613 --> 00:08:23,025
 فَظنَّ الرَّجُلُ بِاَبِيْ

134
00:08:23,251 --> 00:08:27,398
Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) preserved his father and didn't want to kill him.

135
00:08:27,526 --> 00:08:28,738
فَنَفَذتِ الْقَضِّيَّهْ

136
00:08:28,906 --> 00:08:30,175
And the issue was over.

137
00:08:30,545 --> 00:08:34,032
Because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was whispering to Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) and telling him,

138
00:08:34,079 --> 00:08:36,507
 these people are disbelievers, they are worthless.

139
00:08:36,759 --> 00:08:40,639
The blood of any one of them, is no more precious than the blood of a dog.

140
00:08:40,887 --> 00:08:43,077
He's inciting him to do something against his father

141
00:08:43,101 --> 00:08:45,482
but Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) did not take any action.

142
00:08:45,976 --> 00:08:55,348
To the Sahabah(صحابه) men who had dignity, men who had honor, men who had their full trust in Allah

143
00:08:55,840 --> 00:09:04,362
for them to see their Muslim brother taking back to the disbelievers, was disastrous.

144
00:09:05,029 --> 00:09:09,794
This incident of Abu Jandal(أبوجندل) was very difficult for the Muslims to swallow.

145
00:09:10,161 --> 00:09:14,070
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ only did it because he had a promise from Allah.

146
00:09:14,155 --> 00:09:17,705
Because we don't want anybody to argue and say that,

147
00:09:18,165 --> 00:09:20,901
the Muslims could be handed over to the Kuffar(كفار).

148
00:09:21,285 --> 00:09:25,631
This was done because Rasool Allah ﷺ had a promise from Allah.

149
00:09:26,121 --> 00:09:28,982
That Allah will provide them with a way out.

150
00:09:29,057 --> 00:09:34,778
فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ جَاعِلٌ لَكَ وَلِمَنْ مَعَكَ مِنَ الْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ فَرَجًا وَمَخْرَجًا

151
00:09:35,225 --> 00:09:37,958
This was not forecasting by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

152
00:09:37,998 --> 00:09:40,325
This was Wahii(وحي), this is a promise.

153
00:09:40,770 --> 00:09:47,495
Allah will provide you with a way out, Allah will provide you with a solution to your problems,

154
00:09:48,294 --> 00:09:50,212
but it was very difficult on the Muslims.

155
00:09:50,911 --> 00:09:57,006
So, when Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered the Muslims to slaughter their animals and shave their heads.

156
00:09:57,149 --> 00:09:58,101
No one moved!

157
00:09:58,746 --> 00:10:04,222
Yani(يعني) Rasool Allah ﷺ would just point out his order and they would immediately rush to perform it.

158
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:06,595
But this time, suddenly no one moved,

159
00:10:06,823 --> 00:10:12,006
now some scholars tried to say that, this was not disobedience on part of the Sahabah(صحابه).

160
00:10:12,172 --> 00:10:18,362
They were just delaying a bit, with the hope and expectation that may be

161
00:10:18,711 --> 00:10:23,286
Rasool Allah ﷺ would receive a revelation that would change the situation,

162
00:10:23,310 --> 00:10:26,029
and maybe there's still a glimpse of hope,

163
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:27,974
that we might be able to go into Makkah

164
00:10:28,014 --> 00:10:30,585
 because there were so eager to make Tawaf(طواف).

165
00:10:31,133 --> 00:10:34,157
They came with that intention, now they're going back empty handed.

166
00:10:34,387 --> 00:10:37,864
So, they said maybe, if we wait a bit the situation could change.

167
00:10:37,917 --> 00:10:40,999
Rasool Allah ﷺ went back and was very angry, upset.

168
00:10:41,243 --> 00:10:42,464
And he told Ummo Salamah(اُمّ سلمة);

169
00:10:42,789 --> 00:10:46,908
 The Muslims are ruining themselves, I have given them an order and they have disobeyed.

170
00:10:47,337 --> 00:10:51,314
Ummo Salamah(اُمّ سلمة), the wise, Umm-Ul-Momineen(اُمّ الْمُؤمنين) she said;

171
00:10:51,592 --> 00:10:56,653
Messenger of Allah, Do not talk to them about it, they have been under great pressure

172
00:10:56,728 --> 00:10:59,906
because of all the trouble you have taken to achieve this peace settlement.

173
00:11:00,309 --> 00:11:06,081
And because they now realize that they have to take the long way home without achieving their purpose.

174
00:11:06,507 --> 00:11:11,041
And then she told him: If you want them to follow your order go out and do it in front of them.

175
00:11:11,257 --> 00:11:15,574
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ called upon his barber, to cut his hair

176
00:11:15,701 --> 00:11:19,369
and then he would slaughter his animals and his camels

177
00:11:19,409 --> 00:11:24,131
and then all of the Sahabah(صحابه) immediately performed the orders of Rasool Allah ﷺ

178
00:11:24,171 --> 00:11:27,725
but they were very, very sad and depressed state.

179
00:11:28,535 --> 00:11:34,907
The Muslims returned, the whole Hudaybiyya(حُدَيبِية) thing took about between two weeks, 20 days.

180
00:11:35,271 --> 00:11:37,824
On the way, there were two questions on the mind of the Muslims;

181
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:43,471
1) First question was, we were promised that we would make Tawaf(طواف), so what happened.?

182
00:11:44,155 --> 00:11:48,158
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Umar(عُمَر); Did I tell you that you would do it this year.?

183
00:11:48,310 --> 00:11:49,117
Umar(عمر) said: No.

184
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:53,447
Then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him than you would make the Tawaf(طواف),

185
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:58,715
and 2) Second issue: How can we return the Muslims to them,

186
00:11:58,899 --> 00:12:02,384
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said: If we return someone to them,

187
00:12:02,424 --> 00:12:04,509
Allah will provide a way out for them.

188
00:12:04,755 --> 00:12:07,374
If somebody from them comes to us and they're Muslim,

189
00:12:07,543 --> 00:12:10,462
we would send them back and Allah will provide them with the way out,

190
00:12:10,942 --> 00:12:13,182
but if somebody leaves from us to them,

191
00:12:13,575 --> 00:12:15,952
then Allah has rid us from him.

192
00:12:16,071 --> 00:12:18,815
 Why do we want, such a person to remain with us?

193
00:12:19,143 --> 00:12:22,463
Such a person who has given up his Islam and ran away.

194
00:12:22,610 --> 00:12:24,669
Why would we want them to stay with us?

195
00:12:25,128 --> 00:12:29,301
Now, an exception was made to this rule with Muslim woman.

196
00:12:29,919 --> 00:12:32,563
So, Muslim woman are not to be returned.

197
00:12:32,603 --> 00:12:36,523
And there's an Ayah(آية) that was revealed to clarify that issue.

198
00:12:37,247 --> 00:12:41,521
So, is this Ayah(آية) making Naskh(نسخ) of the contract

199
00:12:41,882 --> 00:12:48,758
or is it something that is not explicit in the contract and the Ayah(آية) clarifies it?

200
00:12:48,798 --> 00:12:49,663
Allah Ho-Alam(الله اعلم),

201
00:12:49,783 --> 00:12:51,716
this Ayah(آية) is in Surah Al-Mumtahina(سورة الممتحنة).

202
00:12:52,040 --> 00:13:02,085
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا جَاءَكُمُ الْمُؤْمِنَاتُ مُهَاجِرَاتٍ

203
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:13,144
 إِذَا جَاءَكُمُ الْمُؤْمِنَاتُ مُهَاجِرَاتٍ فَامْتَحِنُوهُنَّ ۖ اللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِإِيمَانِهِنَّ ۖ

204
00:13:13,461 --> 00:13:21,767
فَإِنْ عَلِمْتُمُوهُنَّ مُؤْمِنَاتٍ فَلَا تَرْجِعُوهُنَّ إِلَى الْكُفَّارِ ۖ

205
00:13:22,109 --> 00:13:27,522
لَا هُنَّ حِلٌّ لَهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحِلُّونَ لَهُنَّ ۖ

206
00:13:27,846 --> 00:13:32,774
وَآتُوهُمْ مَا أَنْفَقُوا ۚ

207
00:13:33,036 --> 00:13:42,488
وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْ تَنْكِحُوهُنَّ إِذَا آتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ ۚ

208
00:13:42,862 --> 00:13:54,044
وَلَا تُمْسِكُوا بِعِصَمِ الْكَوَافِرِ وَاسْأَلُوا مَا أَنْفَقْتُمْ وَلْيَسْأَلُوا مَا أَنْفَقُوا ۚ

209
00:13:54,814 --> 00:14:02,125
ذَٰلِكُمْ حُكْمُ اللَّهِ ۖ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ ۚ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

210
00:14:02,372 --> 00:14:06,737
O you, who believe when there come to you believing women, refugees

211
00:14:06,902 --> 00:14:10,833
examine and test them, Allah knows best as to their faith.

212
00:14:11,048 --> 00:14:16,853
If you are ascertain that they are believers then send them not back to the unbelievers.

213
00:14:17,115 --> 00:14:24,000
They are not lawful wives for the unbelievers nor, are the unbelievers lawful husbands to them

214
00:14:24,190 --> 00:14:27,631
but pay the unbelievers what they have spent on their dour

215
00:14:27,897 --> 00:14:33,139
and there will be no blame on you if you marry them on payments of their dour to them

216
00:14:33,423 --> 00:14:36,949
but told not to the guardianship of unbelieving women,

217
00:14:37,229 --> 00:14:40,144
asked for what you have spent on their dour

218
00:14:40,310 --> 00:14:46,674
and let the unbelievers ask for what they have spent on the dours of women who come over to you,

219
00:14:46,752 --> 00:14:53,498
such is the command of Allah, He judges with justice between you and Allah is full of knowledge and wisdom.

220
00:14:54,136 --> 00:14:55,876
So, now to the story of Abu Baseer(أبوبصير).

221
00:14:56,300 --> 00:15:00,271
After the agreement was done, a man called Abu Baseer(أبوبصير)

222
00:15:00,487 --> 00:15:02,328
who belongs to the tribe of Thaqeef(ثقيف).

223
00:15:02,371 --> 00:15:03,285
Where are the Thaqeef(ثقيف) from?

224
00:15:03,325 --> 00:15:07,912
Thaqeef(ثقيف) are from At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف), but he was an ally of Bannu Zahra(بنوزَهْرَة).

225
00:15:08,010 --> 00:15:11,520
And Bannu Zahra(بنوزَهْرَة), are one of the clans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) in Makkah.

226
00:15:11,783 --> 00:15:13,071
Abu Baseer(أبوبصير), was a Muslim,

227
00:15:13,661 --> 00:15:18,910
he fled from the Mushrikeen(مشركين) and he came to Al-Madina(المدينه).

228
00:15:19,609 --> 00:15:25,053
Three days later, two men came asking for him, to be returned.

229
00:15:25,308 --> 00:15:28,299
One of these men is from Bannu Aamir Bin Loaee(بنوعامر بن لؤئي).

230
00:15:28,624 --> 00:15:30,902
One of the branches of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

231
00:15:31,523 --> 00:15:36,014
and the other one was a servant called Kausar(كوثر), who came with him to guide him,

232
00:15:36,579 --> 00:15:42,339
And they had a letter, the letter was presented to Rasool Allah ﷺ, Obae Bin Ka'ab رضي الله عنه read the letter

233
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:45,423
 that, we have an agreement between us

234
00:15:45,969 --> 00:15:49,241
and you have to turn this man back to us.

235
00:15:49,575 --> 00:15:52,490
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) you have to go back.

236
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:53,726
Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) said;

237
00:15:53,766 --> 00:15:58,400
O Messenger of Allah, are you going to send me back to the disbelievers to test me in my religion?

238
00:15:58,596 --> 00:16:00,744
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Baseer(أبوبصير);

239
00:16:01,089 --> 00:16:06,296
We have an agreement with these people and it's not appropriate for us to betray.

240
00:16:07,058 --> 00:16:08,756
وَلَا يَصحُّ فِيْ دِيْنِنَا غَدْرْ

241
00:16:09,159 --> 00:16:11,551
Betrayal is not allowed in our religion.

242
00:16:12,025 --> 00:16:16,128
Rasool Allah ﷺ is not doing this for the Kuffar(كفار), he's not doing it to please them,

243
00:16:16,168 --> 00:16:19,313
he is doing it because these are the rules of Islam.

244
00:16:19,857 --> 00:16:22,527
Even though, the issue relates to Kuffar(كفار).

245
00:16:22,654 --> 00:16:27,884
But these are the virtues and these are the rules of Muslims that we do not betray.

246
00:16:28,204 --> 00:16:29,854
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling Abu Baseer(أبوبصير).

247
00:16:29,894 --> 00:16:33,311
 لَا يَحِّلُّ فِيْ دِيْنِنَا الغَدْرْ، لَا يَصحُّ فِيْ دِيْنِنَا الغَدْرْ

248
00:16:33,444 --> 00:16:37,058
We cannot betray, in our religion, in our religion, this is not allowed.

249
00:16:37,291 --> 00:16:42,456
So, the Muslim is bound by the rules of Allahعَزّوجَلّ in his dealing with Muslims and non Muslims.

250
00:16:42,535 --> 00:16:44,906
We follow the rule of Allah in everything that we do.

251
00:16:45,216 --> 00:16:48,713
And Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) just like he told Abu Jandal(أبوجندل)

252
00:16:48,737 --> 00:16:50,965
that Allah will find a way out for you.

253
00:16:51,587 --> 00:16:53,391
Allah will provide you with a way out.

254
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:55,652
So, now Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) left with these two men.

255
00:16:55,993 --> 00:16:57,972
When they reached to a place called Zul-Khulifah(ذُوالْحليفَة).

256
00:16:58,539 --> 00:16:59,475
There is a Masjid(مسجد) there.

257
00:16:59,515 --> 00:17:02,910
It was Zuhar(ظهر) time, so he, Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) went and prayed two Rak'ah(ركعة)

258
00:17:03,567 --> 00:17:05,897
and he had some dates with him.

259
00:17:06,159 --> 00:17:10,606
So, he told the two men, who came to take him, these Mushrikeen(مشركين),

260
00:17:10,765 --> 00:17:12,005
he said: Come and join me.

261
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:16,009
So, they also brought some bread that they had, and they had a meal together.

262
00:17:16,346 --> 00:17:19,905
This Aamiri(عامري) man, he pulled out his sword,

263
00:17:20,631 --> 00:17:23,479
in one narration it says that, he pulled out his sword and said;

264
00:17:23,942 --> 00:17:29,437
I'm going to use this sort of mine to strike the Aos(أوس) and Khazraj(خزرج) from morning to night.

265
00:17:29,969 --> 00:17:33,071
Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) told him, Is it a good sword?

266
00:17:33,153 --> 00:17:35,298
He said: Yes, it is!. And I have tested it.

267
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:37,698
Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) said: Do you mind, if I see it.

268
00:17:38,418 --> 00:17:42,035
The moment, the sword was in the hands of Abu Baseer(أبوبصير), the man was dead!

269
00:17:42,716 --> 00:17:43,548
That's in one narration.

270
00:17:43,588 --> 00:17:45,821
And other narration it says; they went to sleep,

271
00:17:45,964 --> 00:17:51,839
so Abu Baseer(أبوبصير), his hands were tied, so he pulled out the sword with his mouth

272
00:17:52,426 --> 00:17:58,737
 and then with his mouth holding the sword, he cut the ropes tying his hands,

273
00:17:58,902 --> 00:18:01,828
and then it struck, this Aamiri(عامري) man and kill him.

274
00:18:02,746 --> 00:18:05,196
So, these are the two narrations, that how he killed Aamiri(عامري).

275
00:18:05,598 --> 00:18:11,787
This second man Kausar(كوثر) when he saw that, he just ran away, flying away,

276
00:18:11,882 --> 00:18:13,969
 It says in the narration of Al-Waqedie(الواقدي),

277
00:18:14,242 --> 00:18:18,448
that rocks would fly, from beneath his feet, that's how fast it was going.

278
00:18:18,548 --> 00:18:23,105
and he also says that he raised his Thaub(ثوب), his dress so high,

279
00:18:23,344 --> 00:18:24,851
that his private parts were seen.

280
00:18:24,891 --> 00:18:27,335
I mean, the man was so terrified, he's just flying

281
00:18:27,613 --> 00:18:32,380
and he was not running to the direction of Makkah because it's still far away,

282
00:18:32,420 --> 00:18:34,435
he was running towards the direction of Madina

283
00:18:34,459 --> 00:18:37,007
and Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) was not able to catch him.

284
00:18:37,291 --> 00:18:42,778
I mean, Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) was running after this man, trying to kill him but the man is terrified.

285
00:18:42,966 --> 00:18:46,162
 So, he runs into the Masjid(مسجد) and Rasool Allah ﷺ said: When he saw him.

286
00:18:46,186 --> 00:18:47,301
لَقَدْ رَءَى هَذَا ذؤرا

287
00:18:47,341 --> 00:18:49,301
This man has seen something that terrified him.

288
00:18:49,876 --> 00:18:51,143
They told him: What's wrong with you?

289
00:18:51,295 --> 00:18:54,960
He said: My companion was killed and this man is going to kill me too,

290
00:18:55,216 --> 00:18:57,886
and he was seeking their help.

291
00:18:58,177 --> 00:18:59,927
So, they told him calm down! Don't worry!

292
00:19:00,455 --> 00:19:02,930
Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) came in, holding the sword in his hand

293
00:19:03,177 --> 00:19:04,792
and he told Rasool Allah ﷺ;

294
00:19:04,976 --> 00:19:08,705
 O Rasool Ullah, You have fulfilled your pledge to them,

295
00:19:09,016 --> 00:19:12,571
and you have handed me over to them, you have done your part.

296
00:19:13,348 --> 00:19:15,134
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

297
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:16,103
 وَيْحَ أُمَّهُ

298
00:19:16,143 --> 00:19:19,400
And this part is in Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري), it is authentic.

299
00:19:19,615 --> 00:19:23,678
وَيْحَ أُمَّهُ ، مُسَّعِّرُ الْحَرْبِ لَّوْ كَانَ مَعَه’رِجَالْ

300
00:19:23,953 --> 00:19:29,754
Woe to his mother, he will incite war, if he just had men with him.

301
00:19:30,281 --> 00:19:35,094
The meaning of the statement is that Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) has the capability of starting a war,

302
00:19:35,428 --> 00:19:36,911
if he has men with him.

303
00:19:37,148 --> 00:19:40,359
This statement, what Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) understood from it,

304
00:19:41,246 --> 00:19:44,555
is that Rasool Allah ﷺ is going to hand them over again, if he stays.

305
00:19:44,958 --> 00:19:47,142
So, he decided that he should leave, he left.

306
00:19:47,726 --> 00:19:49,560
Al-Waqedie(الواقدي) by the way, says that

307
00:19:50,088 --> 00:19:54,231
Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) brought, the belongings of Al-Aamiri(ألعامري) to Rasool Allah ﷺ

308
00:19:54,286 --> 00:19:58,037
in order to them divide them, according to the rules of Ghaneemah(غنيمه), the spoils of war.

309
00:19:58,237 --> 00:20:00,463
Rasool Allah ﷺ refused to take them and said;

310
00:20:00,638 --> 00:20:03,860
If I take them then, this is violating my agreement.

311
00:20:04,090 --> 00:20:07,733
It is up to you, to do with it, what you want and Rasool Allah ﷺ refused to take it.

312
00:20:07,780 --> 00:20:12,083
So, Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) is the one who took, what belong to Al-Aamiri(ألعامري).

313
00:20:12,501 --> 00:20:15,002
Now, Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) he cannot go back to Makkah,

314
00:20:15,624 --> 00:20:19,114
he just fled from Makkah and he has killed the man from Makkah.

315
00:20:19,784 --> 00:20:21,330
So, what could he do?

316
00:20:21,537 --> 00:20:24,902
He went to the coast alone.

317
00:20:25,378 --> 00:20:30,078
No one with him, and all what he had with him was a handful of dates

318
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:35,619
and he split up, that small handful of dates

319
00:20:36,343 --> 00:20:39,584
and he ate from it for three days and that was the only food that he had.

320
00:20:40,289 --> 00:20:47,294
Al-Waqedie(ألواقعدي) says that Allah provided for him, on the coast fish that would come to the coast, dead fish

321
00:20:47,334 --> 00:20:51,935
 and he would survive by eating from those fish.

322
00:20:52,426 --> 00:20:56,052
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the story of Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) is amazing.

323
00:20:56,410 --> 00:21:01,727
I mean, a man alone, on the coast with no assistance, with no help,

324
00:21:02,306 --> 00:21:10,483
and there is Ya'ani(يعني), they're looking for him, people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and he is that difficult, fearful situation.

325
00:21:10,731 --> 00:21:16,681
How Allahعَزّوجَلّ provided for him, and gave him a way out, and gave him victory.

326
00:21:17,499 --> 00:21:19,859
 Abu Jandal(اَبُوجَندَل) heard about that,

327
00:21:20,512 --> 00:21:25,394
so he fled from Makkah and joined Abu Baseer(أبوبصير)

328
00:21:25,671 --> 00:21:32,728
and then some other believers who were living under the tyrants, fled and they all joined Abu Baseer(أبوبصير).

329
00:21:33,071 --> 00:21:40,480
And this would make Abu Baseer(أبوبصير), the first Muslim to wage a guerrilla style warfare in the history of Islam.

330
00:21:40,990 --> 00:21:45,901
These men started gathering and there is a narration, According to Al-Waqedie(ألواقعدي).

331
00:21:45,941 --> 00:21:47,761
Al-Waqedie(الواقدي) was one of the scholars of Seerah(سيرة),

332
00:21:47,801 --> 00:21:53,684
 however his narrations do not stand up to the requirements of the Ulema(علماء) of Hadith(حديث).

333
00:21:54,071 --> 00:22:01,075
But he mentions that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) lead a letter writing campaign to the Muslims

334
00:22:01,379 --> 00:22:05,625
 who were living among the Mushrikeen(مشركين) to join Abu Baseer(أبوبصير).

335
00:22:05,736 --> 00:22:08,711
And he mentioned in the letter that Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

336
00:22:08,961 --> 00:22:13,204
Woe to his mother, he would incite war if he just had men.

337
00:22:13,497 --> 00:22:18,806
So, what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) meant by this, is that you men should join him and fight.

338
00:22:18,883 --> 00:22:25,491
Now, they started executing special operations against the caravans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

339
00:22:25,718 --> 00:22:30,663
So, the news of these operations started spread around and now man from Ghaffar(غفار) would join them

340
00:22:30,782 --> 00:22:33,966
 and then men from Johaina(جهينة) and from Aslam(اَسْلَم)

341
00:22:34,125 --> 00:22:36,437
and from the different tribes, all of these young man,

342
00:22:36,477 --> 00:22:40,119
who want to join in this fight in this guerrilla warfare were joining with Abu Baseer(أبوبصير).

343
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:43,079
Until, he had an army of 300 strong,

344
00:22:43,443 --> 00:22:49,950
300 men with Abu Baseer(أبوبصير), and he's leading them in this war against the caravans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

345
00:22:50,031 --> 00:22:53,439
Whenever, they would hear of a caravan of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they would attack it,

346
00:22:53,785 --> 00:22:55,029
take everything in it,

347
00:22:55,239 --> 00:22:58,799
and they would execute everyone in the caravan.

348
00:22:59,528 --> 00:23:02,855
Now, the situation became unbearable for Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

349
00:23:03,101 --> 00:23:04,838
and Rasool Allah ﷺ didn't do anything,

350
00:23:04,878 --> 00:23:07,490
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not involved in this at all,

351
00:23:07,530 --> 00:23:10,918
he did not condemn what Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) was doing, he did not tell him to stop,

352
00:23:11,151 --> 00:23:13,863
Rasool Allah ﷺ was responsible for what was happening in Madina,

353
00:23:13,903 --> 00:23:16,066
he was not responsible for what's happening on the coast.

354
00:23:16,261 --> 00:23:17,806
It's not part of his territory.

355
00:23:17,933 --> 00:23:21,024
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not do anything to stop this

356
00:23:21,278 --> 00:23:25,195
and by the way, when the news reached Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

357
00:23:25,235 --> 00:23:29,069
that Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) has killed the man from Banni Aamir Bin Loae(بني عامر بن لوئي).

358
00:23:29,542 --> 00:23:34,020
Sohail Ibn Amr(سهيل بن عمرو) was very upset because he belongs to his tribe.

359
00:23:34,291 --> 00:23:37,472
So, he put his back on Al-Ka'aba(ألكعبه)

360
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:46,043
and he said, I'm not gonna move my back until the Diyah(ديعة) the blood money is paid for this man

361
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,956
 and Muhammad(محمد) should pay it.

362
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:49,319
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said;

363
00:23:49,414 --> 00:23:50,511
اِنَّ هَذَا لَسَفَاهة

364
00:23:50,551 --> 00:23:52,071
This is insanity!

365
00:23:52,429 --> 00:23:54,398
What does Muhammad(محمد) have to do with this?

366
00:23:54,422 --> 00:23:59,051
Muhammad(محمد) did his part and he refused to allow Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) to stay in Madina and he return them.

367
00:23:59,167 --> 00:24:02,229
Muhammadﷺ did his part, according to the agreement.

368
00:24:02,528 --> 00:24:07,958
So, the Muslims were doing the bare minimum, of what is required from them, in the contract,

369
00:24:08,291 --> 00:24:10,115
 but they're not going to pay any blood money,

370
00:24:10,155 --> 00:24:13,214
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ is not going to tell Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) to stop, what he's doing?

371
00:24:13,466 --> 00:24:17,474
So, Sohail Bin Amr(سهيل بن عمرو) said: Then Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) should pay his blood money.

372
00:24:17,785 --> 00:24:19,872
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) said: And why should Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) pay it,

373
00:24:20,197 --> 00:24:21,624
it is Bannu Zuhra(بنوزُهْرَة) who sent him.

374
00:24:22,144 --> 00:24:23,978
So, he said that Bannu Zuhra(بنوزُهْرَة) should pay it.

375
00:24:24,576 --> 00:24:27,143
Al-Akhnas Bin Shuraiq(ألأخنس بن شريق), who was the head of Bannu Zuhra(بنوزُهْرَة) He said;

376
00:24:27,203 --> 00:24:28,279
We're not going to pay anything.

377
00:24:28,358 --> 00:24:30,730
So, the blood money for this man was lost.

378
00:24:30,803 --> 00:24:32,794
And Sohail Bin Amr(سهيل بن عمرو) received nothing.

379
00:24:32,900 --> 00:24:38,204
See how the Qadar(قدر) of Allah was working things in the favor of the Muslims, and in the favor of Abu Baseer(أبوبصير).

380
00:24:38,460 --> 00:24:44,531
The people of Quraish(قريش), they saw it, as a victory for them in those conditions, in the agreement

381
00:24:44,571 --> 00:24:45,940
 and they would come to regret them.

382
00:24:46,264 --> 00:24:49,068
So now, the situation was unbearable for Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

383
00:24:49,296 --> 00:24:54,458
their caravans they barely took a break and started to breathe fresh air

384
00:24:54,498 --> 00:24:59,412
 and now they're able to do business again, after a few years of war

385
00:24:59,692 --> 00:25:03,285
and now suddenly a new problem comes up and that's the problem of Abu Baseer(أبوبصير).

386
00:25:03,813 --> 00:25:09,564
Because before Abu Baseer(أبوبصير), before Sulh-Hal-Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبيه) Rasool Allah ﷺ was threatening their caravans.

387
00:25:09,654 --> 00:25:14,442
I mean, the Battle of Badr(بدر) occurred because Rasool Allah ﷺ attacked the caravan of Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان)

388
00:25:14,664 --> 00:25:19,045
 and that's what, many of the sarayah(سراية), many of the dispatches, that Rasool Allah ﷺ would send, were

389
00:25:19,085 --> 00:25:24,358
 the purpose and objective of striking against the business roots of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

390
00:25:25,003 --> 00:25:30,412
Now, because of the peace agreement Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) finally will be able to do business again

391
00:25:30,775 --> 00:25:32,976
and they have this problem of Abu Baseer(أبوبصير).

392
00:25:33,199 --> 00:25:36,398
So, they send messages to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

393
00:25:36,994 --> 00:25:42,103
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) see how, they turned into the situation of begging Rasool Allah ﷺ now,

394
00:25:42,419 --> 00:25:46,250
to change those conditions in the agreement.

395
00:25:46,692 --> 00:25:50,588
The conditions which they were insisted on having, included.

396
00:25:50,999 --> 00:25:53,503
Now, they're begging Rasool Ullah and they're asking him

397
00:25:53,618 --> 00:25:54,822
Bisila-Er-Reham(بصلةالرحم), they're saying;

398
00:25:54,862 --> 00:26:00,218
In the name of our relationship, the relationship that we have, we are relatives.

399
00:26:00,499 --> 00:26:03,142
We asked you in the name of the relationship that we have.

400
00:26:03,517 --> 00:26:05,818
That you call these people in.

401
00:26:06,272 --> 00:26:13,769
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ send a letter to Abu Baseer(أبوبصير) inviting them to come back to Madina

402
00:26:13,998 --> 00:26:20,280
and asking the men who belong to the other Bedouin tribes around Madina to go back to their people.

403
00:26:20,554 --> 00:26:22,953
The letter arrived to Abu Baseer(أبوبصير),

404
00:26:23,525 --> 00:26:25,998
when he was in his last moments, he was dying

405
00:26:26,388 --> 00:26:30,044
and he died with the letter of Rasool Allah ﷺ on his chest.

406
00:26:30,563 --> 00:26:33,274
Allah did provide for him a way out,

407
00:26:33,742 --> 00:26:38,135
and Abu Jandal(ابوجندل) returned with the other Muslims to Madina

408
00:26:38,529 --> 00:26:42,264
and this is the promise of Rasool Allah ﷺ that he promised them,

409
00:26:42,295 --> 00:26:44,174
 that Allah will find a way out for you.

410
00:26:44,549 --> 00:26:48,062
The thing is that, the Muslims need to follow the commands of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

411
00:26:48,282 --> 00:26:50,940
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ will provide a way out for them.

412
00:26:51,486 --> 00:26:53,171
We move on to Surah Al-Fath(سورةالفتح).

413
00:26:53,211 --> 00:26:56,059
This Surah(سورة) was revealed on the way back from Al-Hudaybiyyah(ألحديبيه).

414
00:26:56,436 --> 00:26:58,349
It was revealed in its entirety then,

415
00:26:58,753 --> 00:27:03,122
and when it was revealed, Rasool Allah ﷺ send someone to call Umar(عُمَر).

416
00:27:03,383 --> 00:27:06,239
Umar(عُمَر) when he heard that Rasool Allah ﷺ was calling him,

417
00:27:06,550 --> 00:27:11,418
he was afraid that it might be some Ayaat(آيات) revealed, reprimanding him for, what he did.

418
00:27:11,808 --> 00:27:14,013
فَرَجَعْتُ وَاَنْا اَظُنْ اَنَّه’ نَزِّلَ فِيْهِ شَيْء

419
00:27:14,089 --> 00:27:16,615
He was afraid and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

420
00:27:16,700 --> 00:27:21,512
I received Ayaat(آيات), that are better than everything in the world.

421
00:27:22,266 --> 00:27:28,160
نَزَّلَتْ عليَّ الَّيْلَ سُوْرَةْ هِيَّ اَحَبَّ اِلَيَّ مِنَّ الدُّنْيَا وَمَا فِيْهَا، اِنَّ فَتَحْنَالَكَ فَتْحَا مُّبِيْنَا۝

422
00:27:28,983 --> 00:27:31,981
This narration is in Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري), that I mentioned of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

423
00:27:32,005 --> 00:27:37,614
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه he asked Rasool Allah ﷺ, he said;

424
00:27:37,654 --> 00:27:38,629
 اَوَ فَتْحً هُوَ

425
00:27:38,999 --> 00:27:39,947
Is it opening?

426
00:27:40,105 --> 00:27:41,785
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes.

427
00:27:42,085 --> 00:27:45,661
In the name of whom my soul is in His hands, it is an opening.

428
00:27:45,959 --> 00:27:49,500
Now, just an explanation of what the meaning of Fath(فتح) is,

429
00:27:49,679 --> 00:27:51,799
and what the meaning of the word Nasr(نصر) is.

430
00:27:52,112 --> 00:27:53,535
 Fath(فتح) is opening

431
00:27:53,652 --> 00:28:00,698
and it's used in Arabic, the original meaning is used when something is locked and opened, that is Fath(فتح).

432
00:28:00,984 --> 00:28:04,597
So, when a key is put into a lock, and it unlocks it.

433
00:28:04,869 --> 00:28:06,455
That is called Fath(فتح).

434
00:28:06,741 --> 00:28:12,815
This meaning was borrowed, to also mean when a land is open,

435
00:28:13,434 --> 00:28:17,990
because the land is locked against the army.

436
00:28:18,395 --> 00:28:25,042
And it's now opened because it's not like you just walk into the territory of the enemy,

437
00:28:25,340 --> 00:28:27,369
it's locked, it's locked in front of your face,

438
00:28:27,941 --> 00:28:29,594
and you have to fight to open it.

439
00:28:30,118 --> 00:28:36,754
Therefore, the word Fath(فتح) is used to refer to a victory that involves taking over land.

440
00:28:37,208 --> 00:28:42,250
While Nasr(نصر) could be used to refer to victory in a battle.

441
00:28:42,705 --> 00:28:46,118
So for example, if you're talking the victory of Badr(بدر).

442
00:28:46,412 --> 00:28:47,102
You say;

443
00:28:47,189 --> 00:28:48,316
 إِنْتَصَرنَا فِيْ بَدْر,

444
00:28:48,340 --> 00:28:50,411
we were victorious in Badr(بدر).

445
00:28:50,451 --> 00:28:53,977
But you don't say Fatahna Badr(فتحنا بدر) we opened Badr(بدر)

446
00:28:54,165 --> 00:28:56,528
because it was just a battlefield, it wasn't opened.

447
00:28:56,676 --> 00:28:59,068
But you can say Fath-E-Khaybar(فتح الخيبر) or Fath-E-Makkah(فتح مكه).

448
00:28:59,757 --> 00:29:03,322
You can say Fath-E-Makkah(فتح مكه), that Makkah was opened

449
00:29:03,516 --> 00:29:06,680
because there is land that was taken over in the process.

450
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:10,285
So, this is the differentiating meaning between Fath(فتح) and victory.

451
00:29:10,794 --> 00:29:13,502
So, Fath(فتح) has an additional meaning over victory

452
00:29:13,617 --> 00:29:15,567
and that is taking overland.

453
00:29:16,351 --> 00:29:20,469
So, the question is, how could Al-Hudaybiyyah(ألحديبيه) be a Fath(فتح)

454
00:29:20,596 --> 00:29:22,550
when there was no land taken over?

455
00:29:23,236 --> 00:29:25,733
One of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) says, it was called Fath(فتح)

456
00:29:26,370 --> 00:29:30,905
because it is the event that led to the opening of Makkah.

457
00:29:31,064 --> 00:29:34,186
It was because of Hudaybiyyah(ألحديبيه) that Makkah was opened,

458
00:29:34,849 --> 00:29:36,129
and Ibn Masood(إبن مسعود) said;

459
00:29:36,248 --> 00:29:39,520
You think that the opening is, the opening of Makkah

460
00:29:39,709 --> 00:29:42,653
but we used to believe that the opening was the opening of Hudaybiyyah(ألحديبيه).

461
00:29:43,263 --> 00:29:45,078
Why was it an opening? Az-Zohri(اَلزُهْرِي) says;

462
00:29:45,124 --> 00:29:47,439
لَقَدْ كَانَ الْحُدَيْبِيَهْ اَعْظَمَ الْفُتُوْحْ

463
00:29:47,766 --> 00:29:50,185
Al-Hudaybiyyah(ألحديبيه) was the greatest of openings,

464
00:29:50,448 --> 00:29:55,688
وَذَلِكَ اَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم جَآءَ إلَيْهَا فِيْ اَلْفٍ فِيْ اَرْبَعَ مِائة

465
00:29:55,839 --> 00:29:59,267
 فَلَمَّا وَقَعَ الصُلْحْ مَشى النَّاسُ بَعْضَهُمْ فِيْ بَعْضْ

466
00:29:59,340 --> 00:30:04,594
وَعَلِموا وَسَمِعُوا عنِ الله فَمَا اَرَادَه اَحَدٌ الاسْلَامِ اِلَّا تَمَكَّنَ مِنْهُ،

467
00:30:05,062 --> 00:30:10,477
فَمَا مَضت تِلْكَ السَنَتَانْ اِلَّا وَالْمُسْلِمُوْنَ قَدْ جَاوَزُوْاِ إلَى مِائة فِيْ عَشْرَةَ اَلْفْ

468
00:30:10,683 --> 00:30:16,038
That is because Rasool Allah ﷺ came to Al-Hudaybiyyah(ألحديبيه), in a force of 1400.

469
00:30:16,276 --> 00:30:21,102
And when the truce was reached, people started mixing with each other.

470
00:30:21,346 --> 00:30:24,236
And they learned and they heard about Allah.

471
00:30:24,417 --> 00:30:27,740
And anyone who wanted to become Muslim, was able to become Muslim,

472
00:30:28,207 --> 00:30:31,702
because there's now no more threat and fear of becoming Muslim.

473
00:30:32,391 --> 00:30:34,803
So, by the time the two years were over,

474
00:30:35,040 --> 00:30:38,792
the Muslims entered into Makkah in an army of 10,000.

475
00:30:39,052 --> 00:30:42,043
So, in two years, see how the Muslims multiplied

476
00:30:42,813 --> 00:30:48,032
13 years in Makkah and then after that, we have six years until Al-Hudaybiyyah(ألحديبيه).

477
00:30:48,072 --> 00:30:53,841
So, a total of 13 and 6, 19 years and the number was 1400.

478
00:30:54,054 --> 00:30:59,425
In just over two years, the number jumped from 1400 to 10,000.

479
00:31:00,038 --> 00:31:04,378
So, this is the blessing of Sulhal-Hudaybiyyah(صلح ألحديبيه)

480
00:31:04,684 --> 00:31:07,589
that it gave the Muslims a chance to practice Da'wah(دعوة)

481
00:31:07,872 --> 00:31:12,451
because it was a time when there was no risk in becoming Muslim.

482
00:31:12,475 --> 00:31:14,704
And Muslims can travel freely now,

483
00:31:14,939 --> 00:31:17,848
there's no fear so Da'wah(دعوة) spread.

484
00:31:18,604 --> 00:31:22,708
While in Makkah, even though, there was no fighting, but the Muslims were persecuted

485
00:31:23,085 --> 00:31:26,434
and that's why the Da'wah(دعوة) had a difficult time in spreading.

486
00:31:26,745 --> 00:31:30,928
Now, the Muslims had the ability to speak with the people

487
00:31:31,109 --> 00:31:33,844
and the people freely could listen to Islam.

488
00:31:34,961 --> 00:31:35,766
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

489
00:31:35,790 --> 00:31:41,310
إِنَّا فَتَحْنَا لَكَ فَتْحًا مُبِينًا۝

490
00:31:41,874 --> 00:31:45,725
Verily we have granted you and manifest victory.

491
00:31:46,634 --> 00:31:53,884
لِيَغْفِرَ لَكَ اللَّهُ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِنْ ذَنْبِكَ وَمَا تَأَخَّرَ

492
00:31:54,194 --> 00:32:02,188
وَيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكَ وَيَهْدِيَكَ صِرَاطًا مُسْتَقِيمًا۝

493
00:32:02,851 --> 00:32:06,941
That Allah may forgive you, your faults of the past and those to follow.

494
00:32:07,226 --> 00:32:09,631
So, Allah gave Muhammad(محمد) victory

495
00:32:09,729 --> 00:32:14,574
and this victory will be the moment in which Allah will forgive for Muhammadﷺ all of his sins.

496
00:32:14,614 --> 00:32:17,812
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ what sins did he commit.?

497
00:32:18,114 --> 00:32:23,846
We need to understand, put this into perspective, the status of the messenger is very high

498
00:32:23,886 --> 00:32:27,269
and therefore, shortcomings that would come from them,

499
00:32:27,325 --> 00:32:32,155
which for us would seem like doing a great, good deed

500
00:32:32,345 --> 00:32:34,774
because of the highest status of Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء),

501
00:32:35,081 --> 00:32:42,097
what is referred to here as sins, it could be things, that are not appropriate for the highest status of Nabuwwah(نبوَّة).

502
00:32:42,137 --> 00:32:44,460
And these are the things, that Allahسبحانه وتعالى will forgive,

503
00:32:44,484 --> 00:32:47,739
we shouldn't understand these to mean literally sins.

504
00:32:48,347 --> 00:32:50,007
I hope that that meaning is clear,

505
00:32:50,279 --> 00:32:53,364
it is different than what we understand to be sins.

506
00:32:53,795 --> 00:32:59,808
لِيَغْفِرَ لَكَ اللَّهُ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِنْ ذَنْبِكَ وَمَا تَأَخَّرَ وَيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكَ

507
00:33:00,341 --> 00:33:01,908
And fulfill His favor on you.

508
00:33:02,168 --> 00:33:04,379
وَيَهْدِيَكَ صِرَاطًا مُسْتَقِيمًا۝

509
00:33:04,419 --> 00:33:05,587
And guide you on the straight path.

510
00:33:05,683 --> 00:33:07,857
Well Rasool Allah ﷺ was already guided

511
00:33:08,061 --> 00:33:12,979
 but what is meant here is, that there's going to be more laws of Shariah(شريعة) that are revealed,

512
00:33:13,030 --> 00:33:17,627
 and the Ayaat(آيات) will continue being revealed to Muhammadﷺ and that's the guidance.

513
00:33:18,085 --> 00:33:22,687
وَيَنْصُرَكَ اللَّهُ نَصْرًا عَزِيزًا۝

514
00:33:22,883 --> 00:33:26,048
And that Allah may give you, a great victory.

515
00:33:26,429 --> 00:33:28,765
And this great victory is the opening of Makkah.

516
00:33:28,937 --> 00:33:34,343
And what came after that all of the other victories that the Muslims enjoyed after that,

517
00:33:34,667 --> 00:33:36,428
because of the blessing of Sul'hal-Hudaybiyyah(صلح ألحديبيه).

518
00:33:37,430 --> 00:33:44,965
هُوَ الَّذِي أَنْزَلَ السَّكِينَةَ فِي قُلُوبِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ

519
00:33:45,481 --> 00:33:56,112
 أَنْزَلَ السَّكِينَةَ فِي قُلُوبِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ لِيَزْدَادُوا إِيمَانًا مَعَ إِيمَانِهِمْ ۗ

520
00:33:56,501 --> 00:34:04,973
وَلِلَّهِ جُنُودُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمًا۝

521
00:34:05,575 --> 00:34:10,201
It is He will send down tranquility, in the hearts of the believers.

522
00:34:10,655 --> 00:34:16,758
See, the Muslims they came with intention of Umrah(عمرة) and they were returned back

523
00:34:17,036 --> 00:34:20,420
 at a particular moment they gave pledge to die.

524
00:34:20,604 --> 00:34:23,642
So, they prepared themselves, mentally to fight.

525
00:34:23,666 --> 00:34:25,387
And then there was no fighting.

526
00:34:25,507 --> 00:34:28,531
And then suddenly now we have to go back without making Umrah(عمرة).

527
00:34:28,740 --> 00:34:35,997
So, there are a lot of changes that are very difficult to bear that went out within that short period.

528
00:34:36,242 --> 00:34:38,820
Because you prepared yourself mentally for something, you want to do it,

529
00:34:39,104 --> 00:34:41,742
you're prepared to do it, and then you are prevented from doing it,

530
00:34:42,046 --> 00:34:44,615
 you try to do something else, and then you are prevented from doing that.

531
00:34:44,787 --> 00:34:46,663
That causes the state of insecurity.

532
00:34:47,118 --> 00:34:51,082
This state of insecurity Allahعَزّوجَلّ says that it was replaced with Sakeena(سكينة),

533
00:34:51,369 --> 00:34:52,873
tranquility came down.

534
00:34:53,550 --> 00:34:59,072
This tranquility was the understanding that the Muslims now had in the promise of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

535
00:34:59,255 --> 00:35:01,381
that we are coming back victorious.

536
00:35:01,663 --> 00:35:04,576
That Allahسبحانه وتعالى has opened for us.

537
00:35:05,565 --> 00:35:06,948
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

538
00:35:07,054 --> 00:35:15,247
وَلِلَّهِ جُنُودُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمًا۝

539
00:35:15,767 --> 00:35:17,456
Allah(He) is reminding the believers that

540
00:35:18,106 --> 00:35:20,955
to Allah belong the forces of the heavens and earth.

541
00:35:21,138 --> 00:35:26,496
Soldiers of Allah, angels are soldiers of Allah, that came down on the Battle of Badr(بدر).

542
00:35:27,146 --> 00:35:31,088
Wind is a soldier of Allah that was sent from the enemy in Ghazwa-Tul-Khandaq(غزوةالخندق).

543
00:35:31,281 --> 00:35:34,799
Rain is a soldier of Allah that was sent on the Muslims in Badr(بدر).

544
00:35:35,488 --> 00:35:37,805
You don't know who the soldiers of Allah are!

545
00:35:37,829 --> 00:35:39,804
وَمَا يَعْلَمُوْ جُنٌوْدَ رَبِّكَ اِلَّا هُوْ

546
00:35:39,828 --> 00:35:41,887
Only Allah knows, who His soldiers are.

547
00:35:42,394 --> 00:35:46,502
The Momineen(مؤمنين), when they heard the first Ayaat(آيات) of Surat-Ul-Fath(سورةالفتح)

548
00:35:46,854 --> 00:35:50,046
that are promising Rasool Allah ﷺ, those great promises.

549
00:35:50,086 --> 00:35:52,205
 They said that is for you!. What about us?

550
00:35:52,269 --> 00:35:54,405
They were happy for what Allah gave Rasool Allah ﷺ,

551
00:35:54,565 --> 00:35:57,468
and now they want to know what Allah has promised them.

552
00:35:57,570 --> 00:35:58,595
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

553
00:35:58,694 --> 00:36:09,007
لِيُدْخِلَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ

554
00:36:09,308 --> 00:36:18,311
تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا وَيُكَفِّرَ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّئَاتِهِمْ ۚ

555
00:36:18,779 --> 00:36:24,618
وَكَانَ ذَٰلِكَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ فَوْزًا عَظِيمًا۝

556
00:36:25,168 --> 00:36:28,019
That He may admit, the men and women who believe,

557
00:36:28,353 --> 00:36:36,251
to gardens beneath which rivers flow, to dwell therein i.e. forever and remove their ills from them.

558
00:36:36,393 --> 00:36:39,945
And that is in the sight of Allah, the highest achievement for men.

559
00:36:40,933 --> 00:36:43,249
Now, the Ayah(آية) here specifies Mo'mineen(مؤمنين) and Mo'minaat(مؤمنات),

560
00:36:43,329 --> 00:36:49,079
even though when Mo'mineen(مؤمنين) was the masculine form of plural is used,

561
00:36:49,103 --> 00:36:53,489
it's usually refers to both men and women but here's specifically women were mentioned

562
00:36:54,178 --> 00:36:59,065
because the actions that occurred in Sul'hal-Hudaybiyyah(صلح ألحديبيه) were actions of men.

563
00:36:59,239 --> 00:37:03,719
It was men that were going to fight because the battles are fought by men,

564
00:37:03,952 --> 00:37:06,442
but because the Muslim women accompanied

565
00:37:06,744 --> 00:37:11,444
and Muslim women are the ones who have Sabr(صبر) when their husbands leave.

566
00:37:11,569 --> 00:37:15,650
And it is because Muslims women are the ones who take care of their families

567
00:37:15,690 --> 00:37:20,128
when the husband is absent, or when he's killed, Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

568
00:37:20,341 --> 00:37:27,197
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling the Muslim women that they will receive the highest status along with, the men.

569
00:37:27,938 --> 00:37:29,092
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

570
00:37:29,157 --> 00:37:34,353
وَيُعَذِّبَ الْمُنَافِقِينَ وَالْمُنَافِقَاتِ

571
00:37:34,622 --> 00:37:44,323
 وَالْمُشْرِكِينَ وَالْمُشْرِكَاتِ الظَّانِّينَ بِاللَّهِ ظَنَّ السَّوْءِ ۚ

572
00:37:44,789 --> 00:37:49,402
عَلَيْهِمْ دَائِرَةُ السَّوْءِ ۖ

573
00:37:49,624 --> 00:37:59,259
وَغَضِبَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَعَنَهُمْ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُمْ جَهَنَّمَ ۖ وَسَاءَتْ مَصِيرًا۝

574
00:37:59,505 --> 00:38:01,777
We talked about what Allah has given the believers.

575
00:38:01,997 --> 00:38:04,571
And now here Allah tells us what He has given their enemies.

576
00:38:04,922 --> 00:38:07,723
And that he may punish the hypocrites men and women.

577
00:38:07,880 --> 00:38:09,569
So, also the women here were mentioned

578
00:38:09,609 --> 00:38:12,336
because they are supportive of their men

579
00:38:12,686 --> 00:38:18,150
and the polytheist men and women who imagine, an evil opinion of Allah

580
00:38:18,496 --> 00:38:22,639
on them is round of evil, the wrath of Allah is on them,

581
00:38:22,837 --> 00:38:25,400
He has cursed them and God's hell ready for them.

582
00:38:25,463 --> 00:38:27,672
And evil is it, for a destination.

583
00:38:28,314 --> 00:38:31,395
So, here we see that the women of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) are mentioned

584
00:38:31,654 --> 00:38:34,967
and the women of the Mushrikeen(مشركين) are mentioned too.

585
00:38:35,256 --> 00:38:38,268
Because they are the ones, who keep their secrets.

586
00:38:38,367 --> 00:38:42,615
They are the ones who support them, they are the ones who take care of their families in their absence.

587
00:38:42,774 --> 00:38:44,353
So, they share the burden.

588
00:38:44,846 --> 00:38:46,730
Now,  Allah repeats the Ayah(آية) again.

589
00:38:46,846 --> 00:38:55,031
وَلِلَّهِ جُنُودُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَزِيزًا حَكِيمًا۝

590
00:38:55,537 --> 00:38:59,096
For to Allah belongs the forces of the heavens and the earth

591
00:38:59,271 --> 00:39:01,310
 and Allah is exalted and power full of wisdom.

592
00:39:01,634 --> 00:39:05,131
So, this was mentioned with the believers and now it's mentioned with the non believers.

593
00:39:05,378 --> 00:39:08,232
With the believers, Allah has soldiers fighting for them,

594
00:39:08,447 --> 00:39:11,660
and here with the non believers Allah has soldiers fighting against them.

595
00:39:12,226 --> 00:39:13,042
And then Allah says;

596
00:39:13,094 --> 00:39:21,508
إِنَّا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ شَاهِدًا وَمُبَشِّرًا وَنَذِيرًا۝

597
00:39:21,977 --> 00:39:27,678
We have truly sent you, as a witness, as a bringer of glad tidings and, as a Warner.

598
00:39:27,944 --> 00:39:32,075
Here we see three characteristics of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

599
00:39:32,165 --> 00:39:35,295
1) Number one, Shahid(شاهد) witness, and what is the witness?

600
00:39:35,445 --> 00:39:42,035
A witness is someone, who approves or disapproves a claim that is made by someone else.

601
00:39:42,777 --> 00:39:45,221
So, someone goes to court and he makes a claim,

602
00:39:45,428 --> 00:39:49,495
you bring the witness to approve that claim or to disprove it,

603
00:39:49,841 --> 00:39:51,847
and this is the role of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

604
00:39:52,006 --> 00:39:55,807
He will approve the claims of the believers and the non believers

605
00:39:56,119 --> 00:39:57,642
and he will disapprove the claim.

606
00:39:57,928 --> 00:39:59,895
So, he will approve the claims of the believers

607
00:40:00,115 --> 00:40:03,661
and he will disapprove the claims of the non believers.

608
00:40:03,966 --> 00:40:06,435
2) And then the next characteristic is Mubashir(مبشر)

609
00:40:06,603 --> 00:40:08,486
he gives glad tidings to the believers.

610
00:40:08,668 --> 00:40:12,620
3) Wa-Nazeer(ونذير) he delivers, the warnings to the enemies of Allah.

611
00:40:13,097 --> 00:40:21,783
لِتُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَتُعَزِّرُوهُ وَتُوَقِّرُوهُ وَتُسَبِّحُوهُ

612
00:40:22,013 --> 00:40:26,942
وَتُسَبِّحُوهُ بُكْرَةً وَأَصِيلًا۝

613
00:40:27,350 --> 00:40:30,621
In order that you, O men may believe in Allah and His messenger

614
00:40:30,911 --> 00:40:32,761
that you may assist and honor Him

615
00:40:33,137 --> 00:40:35,722
and celebrate His praises morning and evening.

616
00:40:36,320 --> 00:40:39,643
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ talks about Bay'at-Ur-Ridhwan(بيعة الرضوان).

617
00:40:39,863 --> 00:40:49,878
إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يُبَايِعُونَكَ إِنَّمَا يُبَايِعُونَ اللَّهَ يَدُ اللَّهِ فَوْقَ أَيْدِيهِمْ ۚ

618
00:40:50,373 --> 00:40:56,229
فَمَنْ نَكَثَ فَإِنَّمَا يَنْكُثُ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِهِ ۖ

619
00:40:56,444 --> 00:41:04,593
وَمَنْ أَوْفَىٰ بِمَا عَاهَدَ عَلَيْهُ اللَّهَ فَسَيُؤْتِيهِ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا۝

620
00:41:05,050 --> 00:41:11,748
Verily, those who pledge to you, do no less than pledge to Allah,

621
00:41:12,233 --> 00:41:14,316
The Hand of Allah is over their hands.

622
00:41:14,356 --> 00:41:15,294
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

623
00:41:15,406 --> 00:41:20,598
Allah is telling the believers that you did not give your pledge to Rasool Ullah but you gave it to Allah

624
00:41:20,900 --> 00:41:23,662
 and the hands of Allah is above their hands,

625
00:41:24,037 --> 00:41:28,650
then anyone who violates his oath does so, to the harm of his own soul

626
00:41:29,039 --> 00:41:33,068
and the Mufassireen(مفسرين) say; None of these Sahabah(صحابه) violated his oath.

627
00:41:33,092 --> 00:41:38,293
All of these 1400 to give the pledge to Rasool Allah ﷺ, none of them violated their oath

628
00:41:38,627 --> 00:41:42,325
and anyone who fulfills what he has covenanted with Allah.

629
00:41:42,563 --> 00:41:44,955
Allah will soon grant him a great reward

630
00:41:45,366 --> 00:41:52,701
and that's why the ones who gave the Bay'ah(بيعة) to Rasool Allah ﷺ under the tree hold very high status.

631
00:41:53,625 --> 00:41:57,458
Now, notice here that Yubayioonaka(يبايعونك) is used in the present form,

632
00:41:57,538 --> 00:42:03,805
 even though it was a past event and that is to bring this image to us alive,

633
00:42:04,447 --> 00:42:08,567
to show us the importance of what occurred at that moment.

634
00:42:09,491 --> 00:42:21,102
سَيَقُولُ لَكَ الْمُخَلَّفُونَ مِنَ الْأَعْرَابِ شَغَلَتْنَا أَمْوَالُنَا وَأَهْلُونَا فَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَنَا ۚ

635
00:42:21,459 --> 00:42:27,273
يَقُولُونَ بِأَلْسِنَتِهِمْ مَا لَيْسَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ

636
00:42:27,501 --> 00:42:37,442
قُلْ فَمَنْ يَمْلِكُ لَكُمْ مِنَ اللَّهِ شَيْئًا إِنْ أَرَادَ بِكُمْ ضَرًّا أَوْ أَرَادَ بِكُمْ نَفْعًا ۚ

637
00:42:37,728 --> 00:42:42,725
بَلْ كَانَ اللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرًا۝

638
00:42:42,924 --> 00:42:46,603
The desert Arabs, the Aa'raab(أعراب) who lagged behind,

639
00:42:46,762 --> 00:42:51,686
these are the ones who did not come with the believers in Sul'hal-Hudaybiyyah(صلح ألحديبيه).

640
00:42:51,726 --> 00:42:52,778
 Why didn't they come?

641
00:42:53,051 --> 00:42:59,044
they felt that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are too strong and the Muslims will be killed.

642
00:42:59,588 --> 00:43:01,261
So, they stayed behind.

643
00:43:01,838 --> 00:43:05,806
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says the desert Arabs who lagged behind will say to you;

644
00:43:06,063 --> 00:43:12,186
We were engaged in looking after our flocks, and herds, and our families.

645
00:43:12,367 --> 00:43:14,798
So, this the excuse they came forth with,

646
00:43:15,083 --> 00:43:18,289
we stayed behind because of our families and because of our wealth.

647
00:43:18,329 --> 00:43:19,281
Now Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

648
00:43:19,488 --> 00:43:23,642
the 1400 who went with Rasool Allah ﷺ, didn't have any wealth or didn't have any families.

649
00:43:23,797 --> 00:43:26,473
So, this is not an acceptable excuse in the eyes of Allah.

650
00:43:26,642 --> 00:43:30,738
The fact, that you have a family does not excuse you from going out Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

651
00:43:30,880 --> 00:43:35,235
The fact, that you have business to take care of and a job to attend to,

652
00:43:35,650 --> 00:43:38,799
does not excuse you from going Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

653
00:43:39,008 --> 00:43:42,316
So, it's an invalid excuse and then Allah says;

654
00:43:42,586 --> 00:43:47,361
Do thou(you) then ask forgiveness for us, they were asking you to select to forgive them.

655
00:43:47,634 --> 00:43:51,067
They say what their tongues, what is not in their hearts,

656
00:43:51,194 --> 00:43:57,330
say who then has any power at all to intervene on your behalf with Allah.

657
00:43:57,651 --> 00:44:01,761
If His will is, to give you some loss or to give you some profit.

658
00:44:02,164 --> 00:44:04,913
But Allah is well acquainted with all that you do.

659
00:44:05,222 --> 00:44:06,461
And Allah says about them;

660
00:44:06,567 --> 00:44:16,631
بَلْ ظَنَنْتُمْ أَنْ لَنْ يَنْقَلِبَ الرَّسُولُ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ إِلَىٰ أَهْلِيهِمْ أَبَدًا

661
00:44:16,885 --> 00:44:27,113
وَزُيِّنَ ذَٰلِكَ فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ وَظَنَنْتُمْ ظَنَّ السَّوْءِ وَكُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا بُورًا۝

662
00:44:27,346 --> 00:44:29,786
Nay, you thought that the Messenger of Allah,

663
00:44:29,829 --> 00:44:32,269
Allah is telling us the real reason why is, they stayed behind.

664
00:44:32,470 --> 00:44:37,422
Nay you thought that the Messenger and the believers would never returned to their families.

665
00:44:37,733 --> 00:44:41,966
This seems pleasing in your hearts and you conceived an evil thought,

666
00:44:42,204 --> 00:44:44,301
 for you are people lost in wickedness.

667
00:44:44,909 --> 00:44:55,383
وَمَنْ لَمْ يُؤْمِنْ بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ فَإِنَّا أَعْتَدْنَا لِلْكَافِرِينَ سَعِيرًا۝

668
00:44:55,747 --> 00:44:58,653
If any believe not in Allah and His messenger,

669
00:44:58,712 --> 00:45:02,238
we have prepared for those who reject Allah a blazing fire.

670
00:45:02,992 --> 00:45:07,070
وَلِلَّهِ مُلْكُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۚ

671
00:45:07,293 --> 00:45:18,392
يَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَشَاءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَشَاءُ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ غَفُورًا رَحِيمًا۝

672
00:45:18,836 --> 00:45:22,193
To Allah belongs, the dominion of the heavens and the earth.

673
00:45:22,501 --> 00:45:25,417
He forgives whom He wills and He punishes whom He wills

674
00:45:25,638 --> 00:45:27,847
but Allah is oft forgiving, most merciful.

675
00:45:28,640 --> 00:45:39,100
سَيَقُولُ الْمُخَلَّفُونَ إِذَا انْطَلَقْتُمْ إِلَىٰ مَغَانِمَ لِتَأْخُذُوهَا ذَرُونَا نَتَّبِعْكُمْ ۖ

676
00:45:39,465 --> 00:45:44,573
يُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يُبَدِّلُوا كَلَامَ اللَّهِ

677
00:45:45,053 --> 00:45:51,954
قُلْ لَنْ تَتَّبِعُونَا كَذَٰلِكُمْ قَالَ اللَّهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ ۖ

678
00:45:52,248 --> 00:45:56,138
فَسَيَقُولُونَ بَلْ تَحْسُدُونَنَا ۚ

679
00:45:56,336 --> 00:46:01,178
بَلْ كَانُوا لَا يَفْقَهُونَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا۝

680
00:46:01,760 --> 00:46:03,865
Those who lagged behind will say;

681
00:46:04,137 --> 00:46:08,264
when you are free to march and take booty in war, permit us to follow you.

682
00:46:08,336 --> 00:46:09,265
Now Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

683
00:46:09,754 --> 00:46:12,811
they refused to join Rasool Allah ﷺ in Hudaybiyya(حديبية)

684
00:46:13,328 --> 00:46:16,771
because they thought that Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه) will be defeated.

685
00:46:17,499 --> 00:46:21,091
They saw that things were contrary to their belief.

686
00:46:21,644 --> 00:46:26,896
Now, Allah has promised the believers Ghaneemah(غنيمه), spoils of war.

687
00:46:27,174 --> 00:46:29,118
So, these Aa'raab(أعراب) want to join.

688
00:46:29,811 --> 00:46:31,511
For Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) they're willing to join.

689
00:46:31,551 --> 00:46:33,991
When it's for Allah, they don't want to join.

690
00:46:34,508 --> 00:46:35,997
As a punishment for them.

691
00:46:36,121 --> 00:46:39,605
They were prevented from going out with the Muslims in Khaybar(خيبر),

692
00:46:40,334 --> 00:46:41,921
as a punishment for them.

693
00:46:42,571 --> 00:46:44,716
When they were told not to join in Khaybar(خيبر),

694
00:46:45,118 --> 00:46:47,203
they said: You are jealous.

695
00:46:47,592 --> 00:46:49,438
You want to take the spoils for yourself,

696
00:46:49,659 --> 00:46:51,973
يُرِيدُونَ أَنْ يُبَدِّلُوا كَلَامَ اللَّهِ ۚ

697
00:46:52,623 --> 00:46:55,518
So, Allah says those who lagged behind will say;

698
00:46:55,790 --> 00:46:59,314
When you are free to march and take booty in war, permit us to follow you.

699
00:46:59,937 --> 00:47:01,568
They wish to change the Allah's decree.

700
00:47:01,608 --> 00:47:04,155
Say; Not thus Will you follow us?

701
00:47:04,387 --> 00:47:07,155
Allah has already declared this beforehand.

702
00:47:07,635 --> 00:47:10,112
Then they will say but you are jealous of us.

703
00:47:10,341 --> 00:47:13,329
Nay, but little do they understand such things.

704
00:47:13,629 --> 00:47:15,393
These are people who don't have understanding.

705
00:47:15,433 --> 00:47:18,435
 They don't have Fiqh(فقه), their understanding is limited to Duniya(دنيا).

706
00:47:18,718 --> 00:47:22,045
They measure things in dollar sign, that's how they see things.

707
00:47:22,467 --> 00:47:25,777
Everything for them is worldly, they're attached to Duniyah(دنيا),

708
00:47:25,824 --> 00:47:29,353
their hearts are not attached to Allah and not attached to Aakhirah(آخرة).

709
00:47:29,490 --> 00:47:34,354
They do not think about the unseen, they do not think about the future what happens to us after death.

710
00:47:34,576 --> 00:47:37,475
They are limited to the understanding of this Duniyah(دنيا).

711
00:47:38,005 --> 00:47:39,281
A secular way of thinking.

712
00:47:39,662 --> 00:47:41,257
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ telling them;

713
00:47:41,297 --> 00:47:44,876
You see they will be punished from attending Khaybar(خيبر) only but after that they can join.

714
00:47:45,138 --> 00:47:46,195
So, now Allah says;

715
00:47:46,424 --> 00:47:58,809
قُلْ لِلْمُخَلَّفِينَ مِنَ الْأَعْرَابِ سَتُدْعَوْنَ إِلَىٰ قَوْمٍ أُولِي بَأْسٍ شَدِيدٍ تُقَاتِلُونَهُمْ أَوْ يُسْلِمُونَ ۖ

716
00:47:59,398 --> 00:48:04,947
فَإِنْ تُطِيعُوا يُؤْتِكُمُ اللَّهُ أَجْرًا حَسَنًا ۖ

717
00:48:05,115 --> 00:48:14,630
وَإِنْ تَتَوَلَّوْا كَمَا تَوَلَّيْتُمْ مِنْ قَبْلُ يُعَذِّبْكُمْ عَذَابًا أَلِيمًا۝

718
00:48:15,361 --> 00:48:17,767
Say to the desert Arabs, who lagged behind,

719
00:48:17,955 --> 00:48:21,979
you shall be summoned to fight against the people given to wamind war.

720
00:48:22,714 --> 00:48:23,708
أُوْلِي بأسٍ شَدِيْدٍ

721
00:48:23,761 --> 00:48:26,031
they're very tough, in fighting

722
00:48:26,325 --> 00:48:30,417
then shall you fight, or they shall submit?

723
00:48:30,561 --> 00:48:34,228
Then if you show obedience Allah will grant you a goodly reward.

724
00:48:34,366 --> 00:48:36,494
But if you turn back as you did before,

725
00:48:36,818 --> 00:48:39,247
He will punish you with a grievous penalty.

726
00:48:40,196 --> 00:48:43,946
This tough enemy that Allah told them that they will meet.

727
00:48:44,188 --> 00:48:48,386
Some say; It is talking about the Murtaddeen(مرتدين) who followed Musailima Kadhaab(مسيلمه كذاب)

728
00:48:48,672 --> 00:48:52,680
and some say its talking about the Persians and the Romans, Allah-Ho-Alam(الله اعلم).

729
00:48:53,184 --> 00:49:01,715
لَيْسَ عَلَى الْأَعْمَىٰ حَرَجٌ وَلَا عَلَى الْأَعْرَجِ حَرَجٌ وَلَا عَلَى الْمَرِيضِ حَرَجٌ ۗ

730
00:49:02,001 --> 00:49:11,598
وَمَنْ يُطِعِ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ يُدْخِلْهُ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ ۖ

731
00:49:11,980 --> 00:49:17,504
وَمَنْ يَتَوَلَّ يُعَذِّبْهُ عَذَابًا أَلِيمًا۝

732
00:49:17,788 --> 00:49:19,519
No blame is there on the blind,

733
00:49:19,863 --> 00:49:25,907
nor is there blame on the lame, nor on one ill, if he joins not in war.

734
00:49:26,016 --> 00:49:29,041
These are excused from fighting in Jihad(جهاد).

735
00:49:29,655 --> 00:49:35,298
But he that obeys Allah and His Messenger, Allah will admit him to gardens beneath which rivers flow

736
00:49:35,580 --> 00:49:39,185
 and he who turns back Allah will punish him, with a grievous penalty.

737
00:49:39,514 --> 00:49:43,153
And Allah says again the ones, who pledged allegiance under the tree.

738
00:49:43,605 --> 00:49:51,091
لَقَدْ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ

739
00:49:51,297 --> 00:50:01,404
فَعَلِمَ مَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ فَأَنْزَلَ السَّكِينَةَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَأَثَابَهُمْ فَتْحًا قَرِيبًا۝

740
00:50:01,711 --> 00:50:07,271
Allah's good pleasure and that's why this Bay'ah(بيعة) is called the Bay'ah(بيعة) of pleasure, Ar-Ridhwaan(ألرضوان).

741
00:50:07,383 --> 00:50:10,606
Allah's good pleasure was on the believers

742
00:50:10,740 --> 00:50:13,658
when they swore fealty to the under the tree,

743
00:50:14,047 --> 00:50:18,329
He knew what was in their hearts and He sent down tranquility to them

744
00:50:18,770 --> 00:50:22,145
and the rewarded them with a speedy victory.

745
00:50:22,505 --> 00:50:27,787
This tree was a tree that was known after that

746
00:50:27,843 --> 00:50:32,216
and some Muslims would come and pray next to that tree

747
00:50:32,256 --> 00:50:36,838
because of the special occasion that occurred there on the streets mentioned the Quran.

748
00:50:37,287 --> 00:50:42,571
So Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه ordered that, that tree be cut down

749
00:50:43,015 --> 00:50:47,779
because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was worried that this could lead to Shirk(شرك),

750
00:50:48,176 --> 00:50:51,356
it could end up being like Zaat Anwaat(ذات أنواط),

751
00:50:51,846 --> 00:50:53,836
which existed in the time of Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

752
00:50:54,112 --> 00:50:58,416
The people of Jahilliyah(جاهلية) used to think that this tree Zaat Anwaat(ذات أنواط) would give them Barakah(بركة).

753
00:50:58,733 --> 00:51:01,295
 So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) ordered this tree to be cut down.

754
00:51:01,335 --> 00:51:05,343
 Even though, it's a special tree Rasool Allah ﷺ sat under it,

755
00:51:05,628 --> 00:51:08,072
 and the tree is mentioned in Qur'an

756
00:51:08,354 --> 00:51:12,772
but in Islam, it substance not symbols that count.

757
00:51:13,321 --> 00:51:21,523
وَمَغَانِمَ كَثِيرَةً يَأْخُذُونَهَا ۗ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَزِيزًا حَكِيمًا۝

758
00:51:22,372 --> 00:51:24,992
And many gains will they acquire, besides

759
00:51:25,336 --> 00:51:28,711
and Allah is Exalted in Power full of wisdom.

760
00:51:29,212 --> 00:51:33,329
So, Allah promised the believers, bounties.

761
00:51:33,866 --> 00:51:39,802
The first of them was Khaybar(خيبر) and then many other gains will be acquire.

762
00:51:39,826 --> 00:51:45,222
And this is talking about the Ghanaem(غنائم) that the Muslims will win over, until the day of Judgment.

763
00:51:45,988 --> 00:51:57,968
وَعَدَكُمُ اللَّهُ مَغَانِمَ كَثِيرَةً تَأْخُذُونَهَا فَعَجَّلَ لَكُمْ هَٰذِهِ وَكَفَّ أَيْدِيَ النَّاسِ عَنْكُمْ

764
00:51:58,580 --> 00:52:10,416
 وَكَفَّ أَيْدِيَ النَّاسِ عَنْكُمْ وَلِتَكُونَ آيَةً لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَيَهْدِيَكُمْ صِرَاطًا مُسْتَقِيمًا۝

765
00:52:11,271 --> 00:52:14,347
Allah has promised you many gains that you shall acquire

766
00:52:14,653 --> 00:52:20,063
and He has given you these before hand and He has restrained the hands of men from you,

767
00:52:20,306 --> 00:52:22,875
 that it may be a sign for the believers

768
00:52:23,125 --> 00:52:26,105
and that He may guide you to a straight path.

769
00:52:26,761 --> 00:52:32,773
وَأُخْرَىٰ لَمْ تَقْدِرُوا عَلَيْهَا قَدْ أَحَاطَ اللَّهُ بِهَا ۚ

770
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:38,571
وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرًا۝

771
00:52:38,696 --> 00:52:42,414
And other gains there are, which are not within your power

772
00:52:42,504 --> 00:52:44,183
but which Allah has compassed.

773
00:52:44,546 --> 00:52:47,329
And Allah has power over all things.

774
00:52:48,140 --> 00:52:59,398
وَلَوْ قَاتَلَكُمُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوَلَّوُا الْأَدْبَارَ ثُمَّ لَا يَجِدُونَ وَلِيًّا وَلَا نَصِيرًا۝

775
00:52:59,837 --> 00:53:02,661
And if the unbelievers should fight you

776
00:53:02,903 --> 00:53:04,781
they would certainly turn their backs,

777
00:53:05,291 --> 00:53:08,432
then they would neither find protector nor help.

778
00:53:08,796 --> 00:53:11,477
So, if the disbelievers are going to retreat.

779
00:53:11,938 --> 00:53:13,541
Why didn't the Muslims fight them?

780
00:53:13,914 --> 00:53:18,684
Because Allay says that if they would have fought you they would have been defeated.

781
00:53:19,184 --> 00:53:22,840
سُنَّةَ اللَّهِ الَّتِي قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلُ ۖ وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لِسُنَّةِ اللَّهِ تَبْدِيلًا۝

782
00:53:23,145 --> 00:53:26,306
Such has been the practice approved by Allah already in the past

783
00:53:26,611 --> 00:53:29,812
no change will you find to the practice approved by Allah.

784
00:53:30,058 --> 00:53:31,247
So, it's a law of Allah,

785
00:53:31,962 --> 00:53:33,563
that the believers will win,

786
00:53:34,169 --> 00:53:37,413
they might lose in a battle but eventually, they win.

787
00:53:37,932 --> 00:53:38,986
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

788
00:53:39,026 --> 00:53:40,372
 وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنْ

789
00:53:40,412 --> 00:53:46,022
See it's a law of nature just like we have laws of physics and laws of chemistry.

790
00:53:46,046 --> 00:53:48,931
This is a law, believers will win.

791
00:53:49,783 --> 00:53:53,123
They might lose a battle, but they win the war.

792
00:53:53,899 --> 00:53:55,139
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

793
00:53:55,482 --> 00:53:57,815
إِنْ تَنْصُرُوا اللَّهَ يَنْصُرْكُمْ

794
00:53:58,375 --> 00:54:03,860
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will give victory to those who gives support to Allah.

795
00:54:04,694 --> 00:54:05,700
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

796
00:54:05,740 --> 00:54:07,374
 وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنْ

797
00:54:07,398 --> 00:54:10,128
The end belongs to the ones who have Taqwa(تقوى).

798
00:54:10,771 --> 00:54:11,761
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

799
00:54:11,928 --> 00:54:24,070
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ تَنْصُرُوا اللَّهَ يَنْصُرْكُمْ وَيُثَبِّتْ أَقْدَامَكُمْ

800
00:54:25,039 --> 00:54:27,309
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will make your feet firm.

801
00:54:27,924 --> 00:54:30,596
So, the Muslims Yes, they lost in Uhud(أحَد)

802
00:54:30,813 --> 00:54:33,952
but eventually, they won the war against Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

803
00:54:34,229 --> 00:54:37,021
The Muslims might have lost some battles against the Romans,

804
00:54:37,045 --> 00:54:38,397
but eventually they have won,

805
00:54:38,702 --> 00:54:41,599
they might have lost in some battles with the Persians.

806
00:54:41,872 --> 00:54:45,946
But eventually they conquered the entire domain of the Persian Empire.

807
00:54:46,915 --> 00:54:51,327
So, this is a promise from Allahعَزّوجَلّ as long as they are fulfilling

808
00:54:51,456 --> 00:54:54,538
the commands of Allah, and as long as they're believers,

809
00:54:54,804 --> 00:54:58,216
and as long as they are giving Nusrah(نصرة) to the religion of Allah.

810
00:54:58,390 --> 00:55:00,753
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has promised them with victory.

811
00:55:01,136 --> 00:55:05,107
If this is the case, that the enemy would flee,

812
00:55:05,876 --> 00:55:07,036
why didn't they fight them.

813
00:55:07,116 --> 00:55:08,716
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

814
00:55:09,089 --> 00:55:18,750
وَهُوَ الَّذِي كَفَّ أَيْدِيَهُمْ عَنْكُمْ وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ عَنْهُمْ بِبَطْنِ مَكَّةَ مِنْ بَعْدِ

815
00:55:18,941 --> 00:55:27,195
مِنْ بَعْدِ أَنْ أَظْفَرَكُمْ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرًا۝

816
00:55:27,524 --> 00:55:31,045
And It is He! Who has restrained their hands from you,

817
00:55:31,349 --> 00:55:33,953
and your hands from them in the midst of Makkah

818
00:55:34,316 --> 00:55:40,432
after that He gave you the victory over them and Allah see's well all that you do.

819
00:55:41,083 --> 00:55:44,465
We talked about this incident when Kuffar(كفار) sent forty men

820
00:55:44,911 --> 00:55:47,699
in order to take prisoners from the Muslims.

821
00:55:47,935 --> 00:55:52,387
They ended up falling as prisoners in the hands of the Muslims.

822
00:55:52,649 --> 00:55:54,306
And the Rasool Allah ﷺ released them.

823
00:55:55,041 --> 00:55:59,144
So, here Allah is telling us that Allah prevented war.

824
00:55:59,684 --> 00:56:03,482
It was prevented by the Muslims, discovering these kuffar(كفار)

825
00:56:04,041 --> 00:56:07,652
beforehand and that prevented the Kuffar(كفار) from taking prisoners

826
00:56:07,692 --> 00:56:11,426
because if they took prisoners, then war would have occurred

827
00:56:11,673 --> 00:56:20,430
and then Allahعَزّوجَلّ stopped the war by Rasool Allah ﷺ freeing the 40 men from the Kuffar(كفار)

828
00:56:20,470 --> 00:56:24,311
 because if he didn't, then that could have possibly lead to war.

829
00:56:24,808 --> 00:56:28,549
So, why is all of this, why was war prevented ?

830
00:56:29,244 --> 00:56:30,473
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

831
00:56:30,818 --> 00:56:40,781
هُمُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَصَدُّوكُمْ عَنِ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ وَالْهَدْيَ مَعْكُوفًا أَنْ يَبْلُغَ مَحِلَّهُ ۚ

832
00:56:41,302 --> 00:56:56,693
وَلَوْلَا رِجَالٌ مُؤْمِنُونَ وَنِسَاءٌ مُؤْمِنَاتٌ لَمْ تَعْلَمُوهُمْ أَنْ تَطَئُوهُمْ فَتُصِيبَكُمْ مِنْهُمْ مَعَرَّةٌ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ ۖ

833
00:56:57,291 --> 00:57:03,790
لِيُدْخِلَ اللَّهُ فِي رَحْمَتِهِ مَنْ يَشَاءُ ۚ

834
00:57:04,108 --> 00:57:12,046
لَوْ تَزَيَّلُوا لَعَذَّبْنَا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْهُمْ عَذَابًا أَلِيمًا۝

835
00:57:12,973 --> 00:57:17,454
They are the ones, who denied revelation and hindered you from the sacred mosque

836
00:57:17,479 --> 00:57:19,099
and the sacrificial animals.

837
00:57:19,502 --> 00:57:22,144
Detained from reaching their place of sacrifice.

838
00:57:22,547 --> 00:57:28,942
See here, had there not been believing men and believing women,

839
00:57:29,080 --> 00:57:33,033
whom you did not know that you were trampling down

840
00:57:33,637 --> 00:57:38,243
and on whose account, a crime would have accrued to you,

841
00:57:38,373 --> 00:57:41,803
without your knowledge, Allah would have allowed you to force your way

842
00:57:42,493 --> 00:57:44,714
but he held back your hands.

843
00:57:45,488 --> 00:57:48,087
It's because there were some Mo'mineen(مؤمنين) in Makkah

844
00:57:48,880 --> 00:57:51,256
Allahعَزّوجَلّ prevented war from happening.

845
00:57:51,913 --> 00:57:56,859
To save those Mo'mineen(مؤمنين) because of the Muslims made their way through Makkah by force,

846
00:57:57,113 --> 00:58:01,871
there would have been bloodshed and some Muslim men and Muslim women would have been killed

847
00:58:02,101 --> 00:58:09,541
 and that is why the Qadar(قدر) of Allah was to hold back the Muslims and the Kuffar(كفار) from war.

848
00:58:09,861 --> 00:58:13,529
And also Allahعَزّوجَلّ, had a plan for the people of Makkah.

849
00:58:14,166 --> 00:58:17,991
Allah says that He may admit to mercy whom He will.

850
00:58:18,015 --> 00:58:21,933
Many of the people have Makkah were admitted into the mercy of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and they became Muslim.

851
00:58:22,131 --> 00:58:26,097
If the believers would have been apart from the non believers.

852
00:58:26,414 --> 00:58:32,131
We should certainly have punished the unbelievers among them with the grievous punishment.

853
00:58:33,080 --> 00:58:36,719
So, this was the Qadar(قدر) of Allah(الله) that prevented war.

854
00:58:36,828 --> 00:58:39,615
It was not the command of Allah to the Muslims.

855
00:58:39,673 --> 00:58:45,194
This is not Amr Shar'ie(أمر شرعي), it's not a command from Allah to the Muslims not to fight

856
00:58:45,898 --> 00:58:51,471
but it was Amr Qadri(أمر قدري) it was a decree of Allah to the Muslims not to fight.

857
00:58:52,263 --> 00:59:00,680
إِذْ جَعَلَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ الْحَمِيَّةَ حَمِيَّةَ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ

858
00:59:01,133 --> 00:59:09,640
فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِ وَعَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ

859
00:59:09,985 --> 00:59:17,570
 وَأَلْزَمَهُمْ كَلِمَةَ التَّقْوَىٰ وَكَانُوا أَحَقَّ بِهَا وَأَهْلَهَا ۚ

860
00:59:17,737 --> 00:59:22,419
وَكَانَ اللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمًا۝

861
00:59:22,839 --> 00:59:28,141
While the unbelievers got up, in their hearts the heat and kant of ignorance, Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

862
00:59:28,325 --> 00:59:33,044
Allah sent down His tranquility to His Messenger, and to the believers

863
00:59:33,254 --> 00:59:36,937
 and made them stick close to the command of self restraint,

864
00:59:37,298 --> 00:59:40,736
and well were they entitled with, and worthy of it

865
00:59:41,033 --> 00:59:43,257
and Allah has full knowledge of all things.

866
00:59:43,506 --> 00:59:46,337
If the believers would have acted in haste,

867
00:59:47,018 --> 00:59:51,827
then these things that Allahعَزّوجَلّ mentions, Lima'arah(لِمَعَرَّةْ) could have happened.

868
00:59:52,253 --> 00:59:57,852
But they were restrained and they were patient and this was good for them in the long term.

869
00:59:58,102 --> 01:00:03,383
لَقَدْ صَدَقَ اللَّهُ رَسُولَهُ الرُّؤْيَا بِالْحَقِّ ۖ

870
01:00:03,613 --> 01:00:11,436
لَتَدْخُلُنَّ الْمَسْجِدَ الْحَرَامَ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ آمِنِينَ

871
01:00:11,815 --> 01:00:18,945
آمِنِينَ مُحَلِّقِينَ رُءُوسَكُمْ وَمُقَصِّرِينَ لَا تَخَافُونَ ۖ

872
01:00:19,359 --> 01:00:27,756
فَعَلِمَ مَا لَمْ تَعْلَمُوا فَجَعَلَ مِنْ دُونِ ذَٰلِكَ فَتْحًا قَرِيبًا۝

873
01:00:28,476 --> 01:00:33,843
Certainly, Allah has showed to His Messenger, the vision in truth.

874
01:00:34,312 --> 01:00:38,382
You will surely enter Al-Masjid-Al-Haram(ألمسجدالحرام) if Allah wills, in safety.

875
01:00:38,980 --> 01:00:44,353
You remember that we talked about the vision that Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that he's making Tawaf(طواف) in Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

876
01:00:44,394 --> 01:00:46,068
So, Allah is saying that that will happen,

877
01:00:46,208 --> 01:00:50,616
however it didn't happen at that particular time but it will happen in the future and it did.

878
01:00:51,016 --> 01:00:54,531
You will surely enter Al-Masjid-Al-Haram(ألمسجدالحرام), if Allah wills in safety,

879
01:00:54,914 --> 01:00:58,906
with your heads shaved, hair shortened and not fearing anyone

880
01:00:58,960 --> 01:01:01,604
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) when they did make Hajj(حَجْ) with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

881
01:01:01,644 --> 01:01:02,758
They were not fearing anyone

882
01:01:03,103 --> 01:01:05,659
when that happened in Hajjah-Tul-Wida'a(حجة الوداع), the farewell Hajj(حَجْ).

883
01:01:05,918 --> 01:01:12,749
He knew, what you did not know and has arranged for that a conquest near at hand.

884
01:01:13,230 --> 01:01:14,524
And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

885
01:01:14,642 --> 01:01:23,985
هُوَ الَّذِي أَرْسَلَ رَسُولَهُ بِالْهُدَىٰ وَدِينِ الْحَقِّ لِيُظْهِرَهُ عَلَى الدِّينِ كُلِّهِ ۚ

886
01:01:24,215 --> 01:01:27,398
وَكَفَىٰ بِاللَّهِ شَهِيدًا۝

887
01:01:27,586 --> 01:01:34,900
It is He, Who send His messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to manifest it, over all religion

888
01:01:35,304 --> 01:01:37,733
 and sufficient is Allah as witness.

889
01:01:38,057 --> 01:01:45,991
Allahعَزّوجَلّ tells us that the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ that was sent through Muhammadﷺ

890
01:01:46,413 --> 01:01:51,621
and the guidance that was sent with Muhammadﷺ, will manifest over all religion

891
01:01:51,875 --> 01:01:53,278
 and then the last Ayah(آية),

892
01:01:53,530 --> 01:02:01,506
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says and this is in Ayah(آية) that is continuous virtues for the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

893
01:02:01,694 --> 01:02:05,683
مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ۚ

894
01:02:05,802 --> 01:02:14,046
وَالَّذِينَ مَعَهُ أَشِدَّاءُ عَلَى الْكُفَّارِ رُحَمَاءُ بَيْنَهُمْ ۖ

895
01:02:14,351 --> 01:02:16,195
Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah,

896
01:02:16,468 --> 01:02:22,948
and those who are with him are forceful against the disbelievers, merciful among themselves.

897
01:02:22,988 --> 01:02:28,670
 Remember, we said that the disbelievers refused to write down Muhammad(محمد) Rasool(رَسول) Allah(الله),

898
01:02:28,710 --> 01:02:30,235
 that he is the Messenger of Allah,

899
01:02:30,892 --> 01:02:34,448
they refused to testify and witnessed that he is the Messenger of Allah.

900
01:02:34,488 --> 01:02:36,359
 So, Allah revealed it, in Qur'an

901
01:02:36,571 --> 01:02:41,212
that Allah has sent Muhammadﷺ as a Messenger and Muhammad(محمد) is Rasool Ullah(رسول الله)

902
01:02:41,800 --> 01:02:45,776
and here we have characteristics of the Sahabah(صحابه).

903
01:02:46,185 --> 01:02:50,330
Number one, they are forceful against the disbelievers,

904
01:02:50,709 --> 01:02:51,783
رُحَمَاءُ بَيْنَهُمْ ۖ

905
01:02:51,862 --> 01:02:53,759
and they are merciful among themselves.

906
01:02:53,799 --> 01:02:59,892
Unfortunately, we find that, there are some Muslims who are the total opposite of this description.

907
01:02:59,948 --> 01:03:04,829
So, they are forceful against the believers and they are very merciful towards the disbelievers.

908
01:03:05,717 --> 01:03:14,129
تَرَاهُمْ رُكَّعًا سُجَّدًا يَبْتَغُونَ فَضْلًا مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرِضْوَانًا ۖ

909
01:03:14,551 --> 01:03:21,015
You see them bowing and prostrating in prayer seeking bounty from Allah and His pleasure.

910
01:03:21,086 --> 01:03:24,598
 So, one of the most prominent characteristics is their Salah(صلاة).

911
01:03:24,686 --> 01:03:29,536
 You find them, you look at them, you will see that, they are in Sujood(سجود) or they are in Rakooh(ركوع),

912
01:03:29,841 --> 01:03:35,512
سِيمَاهُمْ فِي وُجُوهِهِمْ مِنْ أَثَرِ السُّجُودِ ۚ

913
01:03:35,660 --> 01:03:39,457
Their mark is on their faces from the trace of prostrations.

914
01:03:39,497 --> 01:03:44,453
So, prostration leaves a trace on the face, it's not talking about the dark mark that is on the forehead

915
01:03:44,477 --> 01:03:48,475
it's talking about the light that shines from the face because of Sujood(سجود).

916
01:03:48,942 --> 01:03:52,784
ذَٰلِكَ مَثَلُهُمْ فِي التَّوْرَاةِ ۚ

917
01:03:53,167 --> 01:03:56,045
That is their description in the Taurah(توراة).

918
01:03:56,349 --> 01:04:04,360
وَمَثَلُهُمْ فِي الْإِنْجِيلِ كَزَرْعٍ أَخْرَجَ شَطْأَهُ فَآزَرَهُ فَاسْتَغْلَظَ

919
01:04:04,709 --> 01:04:14,574
فَآزَرَهُ فَاسْتَغْلَظَ فَاسْتَوَىٰ عَلَىٰ سُوقِهِ يُعْجِبُ الزُّرَّاعَ لِيَغِيظَ بِهِمُ الْكُفَّارَ ۗ

920
01:04:14,973 --> 01:04:25,250
وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ مِنْهُمْ مَغْفِرَةً وَأَجْرًا عَظِيمًا۝

921
01:04:26,655 --> 01:04:33,782
And their description in the Gospel is, as a plant which produces its offshoots and strengthens them.

922
01:04:33,822 --> 01:04:38,256
 So, they grow firm and stand upon their stocks the lighting the sowers,

923
01:04:38,391 --> 01:04:45,237
so that He(Allah) may enrage by it, them, the disbelievers.

924
01:04:45,346 --> 01:04:53,044
Allah has promised those, who believe and do righteous deeds among them forgiveness and a great reward.

925
01:04:53,487 --> 01:04:58,431
So, the analogy or the similitude of the believers in the Gospel is

926
01:04:58,471 --> 01:05:06,970
like a plant that grows until, it is firm and it is unbreakable and that angers the disbelievers.

927
01:05:07,412 --> 01:05:10,445
These are the Ayaat(آيات) of Surat-Ul-fath(سورةالفتح) that were revealed

928
01:05:10,867 --> 01:05:14,881
after this great opening of Sul'ha Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبية).

929
01:05:15,264 --> 01:05:20,273
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

930
01:05:20,660 --> 01:05:23,408
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُه’

